{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review","id":1541228,"title":"W5 Shattered Nation - Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-30T08:23:16-07:00","id":1541228,"title":"W5 Shattered Nation - Review","content":"There\u2019s a tagline on the product-page for Shattered Nation. It says \u201cThe society of Garou unveiled.\u201d. In that sense it seems quite obvious what the book is trying to do. But what the book is actually doing is somewhat more complicated.<br /> <br /> Three strands show up in this effort to \u201cunveil Garou society\u201d. The first is to revise or expand information given by the W5 corebook. The most pronounced example of this is Chapter Five: Speaking With The Enemy. Rather than simply introducing new allies and antagonists or offer new story-hooks for existing ones, this chapter re-examines ALL the categories of beings in the corebook\u2019s \u201cAllies and Antagonists\u201d-chapter and gives different or more nuanced takes on all these categories. The second strand that stands out is that this book is liberally borrowing from legacy-material. Sept-positions, howls, Rites that are new to W5, references to things like the Under The Blood Red Moon book, the Storm Eater, the Amazon war and of course a lot of stuff about Jonas Albrecht as an older (and broken) version of legacy Jonas Albrecht\u2026 It\u2019s all legacy-material. The third strand is that the book\u2019s proposed concept of a \u201cfallen Garou Nation\u201d can be summarized like this: \u201cIt\u2019s a wolf-eats-wolf-world and it\u2019s every Sept for themselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> This is what is going on and there\u2019s good stuff in this book. But before I get to a beat-by-beat review of this book, to finish this introductory summary there are three glaring issues that plague this book. The first comes with that that third strand I mentioned, the \u201cevery Sept for themselves\u201d-aspect. So you get talk of how a PC relates to their Pack, how the Pack relates to the Sept, how Septs relate to each other and how Spirits figure into this. But there\u2019s something big missing from this: The Tribal perspective. Hell, you get more of a perspective on Black Spiral Dancers, the Cult of Fenris and Stargazers in the aforementioned Chapter Five than on any of the other Tribes. Garou are mentioned and the Tribes they belong to always feel more incidental than anything. And other than that, it\u2019s just this obvious stuff like Children of Gaia Garou being community-minded and longing for peace, Silent Striders being fans of travel and Silver Fangs being arrogant. But you never get any dedicated sections exploring how Tribes figure into this fallen-Garou-Nation-setting. The second issue is that while this book introduces all these references to legacy-material, it can\u2019t completely leave the ahistorical \u201cWho knows?\u201d-mystification behind. So you get a reference like the Storm Eater and it\u2019s this half-hearted summary because it has to come with an asterisk saying \u201cWho knows what really happened?\u201d. But if you so obviously borrow from legacy-material and you only present like 70% of the story then any person is just one google-search away from just looking this up on the White Wolf Wiki and getting the whole story anyway. So why even bother with this whole charade at that point? Since you\u2019re 70% of the way to a whole copy-paste-affair already, why not go the whole nine yards? The third and last big issue with this book is that there\u2019s quite a bit of in-character talk, lengthy quotes, dialogues, speeches\u2026 there are a lot of pages dedicated to this. And in theory I welcome that. It\u2019s a great idea and provides an opportunity to give the W5 more flavor. But here\u2019s the thing: The in-character writing in this book is terrible. Most of the characters are either annoying and/or deeply unlikeable. Honestly, I\u2019d probably leave the Garou Nation as well if Garou are like this in W5. For example, old Jonas Albrecht in how he\u2019s presented in this book is this cranky, self-important old man that according to this book, I shit you not, walks with a walking-stick that he beats people with if he feels that they don\u2019t respect him enough. And the writing itself\u2026 oh god\u2026 there\u2019s a scene where a Pack is summoning an Ancestor-Spirit\u2026 That one really tested my patience. It had lines like this (which is supposed to be part of the summoning): \u201cSweet flesh we hunted. TOCH AROUH. Our life. Humans call it \u201canimism\u201d or some shit. We call it tradition.\u201d And since the Ancestor Spirit is an indigenous person while the Garou are not, phrases like \u201ccolonialist guilt\u201d are thrown around. But then these phrases are embedded in these abrasive comments. It just feels tonally off.<br /> <br /> And speaking of bad writing\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Introduction - Low Growl Speaks\u2026</span><br /> <br /> The Introduction starts with a bit of in-character-writing. Low Growl is a wolf-born Silent Strider Philodox (she\u2019s later featured in a character-section as well). It\u2019s about this Garou making a speech at a Moot and trying to gather support for a mission. It starts like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last night, this moot opened with a grand tale of woe. A Galliard speaking with the voice of the most beautiful of songbirds \u2013 yes, you there , hi \u2013 told us of the final days of the Garou Nation. The Last Grand Convo\u2026 Conco\u2026<br /> <br /> (Someone shouts: Concolation!) Yes! That. One of those really big moots where the important issues facing all Garou were decided. Bear with me, okay? I\u2019m trying to talk fancy since this is a moot and you\u2019re all so eloquent.<br /> <br /> (Laughter, not all derisive)<br /> <br /> The Last Concolation was where King Albrecht was supposed to have nominated a successor. Instead, his rule was challenged by the Shadow Lords, the Red Talons, the Galestalkers, even the Hart Wardens \u2013 to say nothing of the Septs and Packs clamoring for action. So many young Garou who\u2019d never been to such a moot before eager to hear from their king.<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t there and the first I heard of all this was yesterday. You-<br /> <br /> (Low Growl pointing at the Galliard in the audience)<br /> <br /> - Put this in sweeter words. But what I heard was that a bitter old man had nothing to offer those who were not even born in his glory days.<br /> <br /> Why did the Garou Nation fall? Why did that Concolation become the last time we\u2019d come together?<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t ask me! I was born a wolf, so all these stories from the youth of our elders are ancient history to me! </div> </div> </div>You got a few key parts of this book right there. You\u2019ve got information about this Last Grand Concolation where it all went south for the Garou Nation (there are other in-character quotes in the book that add more detail to what was going on like more than just the mentioned challenge, this was also the event where the Fenrir left) and most importantly you have the paradoxical relationship this book has with the fallen Garou Nation. The characters in this book and the attitudes represented all clamor for something like the Garou Nation, a state of things where unity, cohesion and cooperation are assured. Where it becomes paradoxical is that at the same time all the characters in this book (who are old enough to remember the Garou Nation) are convinced that the Garou Nation sucked and it was never all that useful.<br /> <br /> The sample of the writing is also an indicator what all in-character-writing is like in this book. The tone\u2019s abrasive, irreverent and vulgar but it doesn\u2019t come with the sort of wit or humor to make this bearable to read. There are some side-characters like Lil Sister who are different but they only feature as characters in dialogues. The main-voices you hear in this book are similar to how Low Growl speaks in this Introduction.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Chapter One: Strength In The Pack</span><br /> <br /> This chapter is focused on Pack Types and gives advice on creating Packs and what sorts of complex actions Packs can undertake. Overall, a good chapter that both offers new options to players as well as offers some good advice for session-zero.<br /> <br /> It starts by talking about Pack-dynamics and it does that by offering four key-issues and then presents three options for how a Pack addresses that. First, you have how the Pack treats each other (you get \u201cThe Family\u201d, \u201cTeam of Rivals\u201d and \u201cThe Professionals\u201d). Then you have the Pack\u2019s relationship to the world of Spirits (you got \u201cCautious\u201d, \u201cCurious\u201d and \u201cProblem Solvers\u201d). A concept that I think should\u2019ve been covered in far more detail by the book is that the next issue is the Pack\u2019s relationship to the Veil (you got \u201cVeil Lowered\u201d, \u201cVeil Parted\u201d and \u201cVeil Lifted\u201d). What this proposes is that in W5 you have approaches ranging from \u201cWe honor the Veil and keep things secret.\u201d to \u201cWe regularly talk to our human allies and tell them everything.\u201d. The last bit is the Pack\u2019s relationship to the Sept (you got \u201cThe Linchpin\u201d, \u201cThe Iconoclasts\u201d and \u201cThe Outsiders\u201d). All in all, it\u2019s a good outline to go through with players about what kind of Pack they wanna play. Something that comes up quite often in this book, though, is that options are getting discussed here that are so broad and general that it doesn\u2019t feel like it warrants the wordcount that it gets. Likewise here, because I think outside of the Veil-section, it\u2019s pretty much all what you think it is. And yet all these options get these explanations with dozens of words each.<br /> <br /> Next we get to the introduction of the new Pack Type system. It\u2019s good, although there are some issues that I think you\u2019d immediately have noticed if you had playtested this. It\u2019s similar to the Coterie-system by having its own set of attributes. You got Territory, Community and Spirit. Territory isn\u2019t the amount of area you control but rather measures the health of the land. Community is about how closely the Pack is integrated into human society. And Spirit\u2026 well, that one\u2019s the weakest one because of how vague it is. It isn\u2019t the Pack\u2019s knowledge of the Umbra and the local spirits but rather a kind of \u201cgut instinct\u201d the spirits have when they encounter the Pack. How or why this happens is left unexplained. You can use these ratings as a once per session dice bonus effect when it\u2019s applicable. So far so good. What I found a bit mystifying is that the book is overly concerned right here about players stacking dice-boni and you get these exceptions for all three for what you can and can\u2019t add as dice-boni at the same time. Like with Spirit, for example, the text is making clear that you can either use your Renown-bonus for a social roll while interacting with a spirit OR the Spirit-dice-bonus from the Pack-Type but not both at once. Honestly, who cares if a player decides to do both at the same time\u2026 As long as it makes sense, why not?<br /> <br /> Then it talks about pooled Backgrounds and Flaws which is also the moment where W5 introduces Patron-Spirits for Packs. The idea is that you use Spirit Pact as a pooled Background and at three dots you get a \u201cGuiding Spirit\u201d for the Pact. This is how the book explains it: \u201cAt the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, Guiding Spirits at three dots or above may provide the pack with a minor version of a Favor and Ban for as long as the pact exists. The Favor is a one-die bonus to a single kind of test in the spirit\u2019s purview once per session. The Ban is a separate action related to the opposite of the spirit\u2019s purview that requires spending a Willpower point to perform it after invoking the Favor. For example, a flame spirit might grant a onedie bonus to withstanding moving through a burning environment but might require spending a Willpower point to put out any of those fires.\u201d That still leaves a bit of work to the ST to make this work, of course. And I was surprised that the book never acknowledges how this is supposed to interact with the Rite of Patronage (pg 184) from the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> Where it gets a bit silly is in how it explains the amount of dots you get. First, it says that with two players you get three dots per player, with three players two dots per player and with four and more you get one dot per player. I\u2019m pretty sure there\u2019s a simpler way to present this. Obviously, the standard is six dots and with five and more, you might want to raise it. Then it gets even sillier when it says that you have to put at least one dot in each of the three aforementioned Pack Type attributes (unless you play a nomadic Pack which has 0 in Territory). So, effectively, the actual amount of points you get to spend is three. Then you can take up to four dots in Flaws which gives you four extra dots to spend on Pack-stuff. This is relevant because nearly ALL the listed examples for Pack Types in this book take four dots in flaws. Even worse, in 90% of the cases, it\u2019s four dots in either Enemies or Adversary. Personally, I would feel like something has gone wrong here conceptually when the listed examples make it feel like four dots in Enemies or Adversary is some sort of auto-take for this process.<br /> <br /> The list of listed Pack-Type is quite long with 15 given examples. On one hand, that\u2019s good but when you\u2019re gonna hear what they\u2019re like, you\u2019ll realize that most of them are quite bland conceptually. In my opinion, most players should be expected to come up with broad concepts like these on their own.<br /> <br /> The listed Pack-Types are: Activists (the Pack has attached themselves to a human activist cause), Avengers, Banishers, Caern Guard, Couriers, Diplomats, Evangelists for Luna, Hell Raisers (the Pack has attached themselves to a particular subculture movement), Monkeywrenchers, Occultists, Penitents, Reformers (the Pack wants to rebuild the Garou Nation in a reformed state), Scavengers, Veil Keepers and Watchers (Garou policing other Garou).<br /> <br /> To showcase what these Pack-Type descriptions are like (and show off the only truly interesting one), here\u2019s what Evangelists for Luna is like:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Evangelists for Luna</b><br /> Moon Cults dedicate themselves to the service of Luna, the spirit of the Moon and Gaia\u2019s sister. They venerate her in the same way that other Garou do Gaia, and some even go as far as to declare that doing so is the only natural response if Gaia is indeed dead or dying. While Moon Cults aren\u2019t considered fallen or actual enemies, to say that theirs is a controversial belief among Garou society is an understatement.<br /> Some septs outright forbid Moon Cults from visiting their caerns, let alone joining them. Still, Moon Cults are on the rise with younger Garou, and rumor has it at least one sept is made up entirely of Moon Cult packs. When the troupe chooses this pack type, every player must decide on three beliefs about Luna that the pack holds. This is their Moon Cult doctrine. This doctrine is not universal; while Moon Cults respect each other, they tend to have their own beliefs about Luna, her new role in the world with Gaia\u2019s decline, and how Garou should best serve her.<br /> - Territory \u2022\u2022<br /> - Community \u2022<br /> - Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> - Spirit Pact (\u2022\u2022\u2022, a spirit related to the cult\u2019s doctrine, Power 2, Host)<br /> - Spirit Pact Flaw: Pact Condition (\u2022, adds one dot to the pack pool)<br /> - Adversaries (\u2022\u2022, a rival Moon Cult or an orthodox pack that despises the pack\u2019s doctrine, adds one dot to the pack pool)<br /> Possible Extras: Allies (Human adherents who don\u2019t know the truth), Mentor, Resources<br /> <br /> <br /> It feels a bit like cheating that this book mentions Moon Cults a few times but as you can see here, the details are pretty much up to the people at the table to figure out. Also, if you\u2019re gonna make them pick three Moon Cult doctrines, it should be mentioned that there\u2019s another part of the game that also already is kind of about picking three doctrines: Chronicle Tenets. I think it would be reasonable to just do both at the same time in a situation like this one. The text also highlights the strange thing where the listed Pack Types seem to think that Flaws only give you half their value (rounded up) in extra dots to the Pack-Type-dot-pool which isn\u2019t the case. Lastly, that \u201cPossible Extras\u201d-bit there never felt worthwhile because of how obvious it was. Similar to how a lot of the listed Pack-Types are way too broad to be particularly interesting as an example, these \u201cPossible Extras\u201d are also way too obvious. Most of the listed Pack Types in this book just lack flavor. They should\u2019ve brought back Pack-Types from other supplements that feel more interesting (like the mentioned Pack-Types in Scent of Decay where everybody has the same Auspice, for example).<br /> <br /> Next we get to Pack Actions which starts normal but gets weird fast. It starts with \u201cOrganize an Ambush\u201d and you think \u201cOkay, I can see that. You\u2019d do something like that as a Pack.\u201d. Then you get \u201cReconnaissance\u201d which is already a bit odd because the \u201cOrganize an Ambush\u201d-section already talked about how you should scout out your enemy but okay, so it goes into more detail on that aspect. Next Pack Action: \u201cGuard Local Human Environmental Activists\u201d. Suddenly things have gotten VERY specific! Here\u2019s a quote from the section: \u201cThey are Earth liberationists, anarcho-primitivists, and green anarchists fighting to stop deforestation, oil drilling, the coming of the end. When the work of human activist groups aligns with the goal of the Garou, it makes sense to protect them, to help them keep fighting. Politics can be a very useful Skill to understand the big picture. Awareness may alert of an incoming attack and Medicine help keep humans alive in its aftermath.\u201d I get the part where when your human allies come under attack, you protect them \u2013 but how is that a distinct \u201cPack Action\u201d? That\u2019s obviously more of a reaction to what the bad guys are doing.<br /> <br /> But it gets crazier! Next up in the list of Pack Actions we have: \u201cKidnap a local politician\u201d. I had a bit of a double-take reading that. \u201cKidnap a politician\u201d\u2026? This book thinks one way for Packs to take action is to \u201ckidnap politicians\u201d\u2026? First of all, how is this even supposed to work? I can understand kidnapping somebody close to the politicians to blackmail/pressure/manipulate them. But if you want the politician to do something how is kidnapping them supposed to help? Obviously they can\u2019t do anything for the Garou while they\u2019re kidnapped. It makes sense to kidnap a higher-status person if all you\u2019re after is a ransom. But if you want particular higher-status people to do a particular thing, kidnapping them isn\u2019t going to help a lot (unless you have some supernatural means to make them keep their word). You can make them pinky-swear that they ought to do a particular thing and if I were the ST, the first thing that person would do upon release is call the cops instead. If it\u2019s just for the sake of gaining information, kidnapping is a very drastic move (that also attracts a lot of attention). The writing in this section is particularly cringe-worthy as well (it reminded me of the Ahroun-section in the corebook) with lines like &quot;Kidnapping public figures is risky business, no shit.&quot; or passages like &quot;Congratulations. You have a fundamentalist politician strapped to a chair in your aunt\u2019s Airbnb. Now it\u2019s time to expose his corruption, state your demands, negotiate his release, and hope to Luna the vacation rental won\u2019t get booked.&quot; (also, again, who are you stating your demands to...? You've already kidnapped the target of such a pressure-campaign...).<br /> <br /> Next we got \u201cBlow It All Up\u201d which is what it says\u2026 Again, seems a bit obvious. I don\u2019t think this needed to get dozens of words and its own subsection. After that you have \u201cClaim and secure your territory\u201d which is way too broad to be useful. Then you got \u201cCall a Moot\u201d which wasn\u2019t necessary because the book gets into that in more detail later on. This is followed by \u201cSabotage the Infrastructure of Entropy\u201d which is just \u201cBlow It All Up\u201d again except this time the text acknowledges that you can do more than just literally blow things up if you want to take down Pentex-supported corporations. Then you got another weird one with \u201cForm an (Unlikely) Alliance\u201d because as I mentioned at the start, this book has an entire chapter later on about this very thing!<br /> <br /> After the ambush-bit and reconnaissance, this section on Pack Actions just kinda went off the rails. In my opinion, whoever wrote this section didn\u2019t understand the assignment and what a section called \u201cPack Actions\u201d should\u2019ve been about. Besides the first two, everything veered between irrelevant, too broad, too specific and just plain odd here. This wasn\u2019t helpful at all!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Chapter Two: Among Wolves</span><br /> <br /> This chapter discusses Garou society and presents some example Garou and Septs. It starts by emphasizing the \u201cevery Sept for themselves\u201d-aspect and you get a table with ten examples for why two Septs dislike each other. It\u2019s not that useful because I think most STs could easily figure out why two Garou-Septs dedicated to the War against the Wyrm might\u2019ve grown to dislike each other or run into some issues that aggrieved one or both parties.<br /> <br /> Then we get a section on Generations where the book doubles down on all the \u201cWho knows\u201d-mystification and tries to explain it. It still isn\u2019t convincing in my opinion. The main-thrust of the argument relies on this notion: \u201cThe quick succession of generations means that a Garou in their thirties might already be considered a grizzled veteran, someone who survived when so many did not. At a typical sept, only a minority of the Garou make it past ten years as a Garou.\u201d And this then gets cemented by a description of the Garou\u2019s sense of time and history: \u201cThe Garou are creatures of the present, their traditions built on oral storytelling. This means that factual accuracy is often not considered particularly important as long as the broad outlines fit what the crowd at the moot wants to hear. The stories of Garou from the '80s and '90s are already ancient history, having happened before most Garou today were even born. Garou legends are notoriously difficult to date accurately. When was the War of Rage or the Impergium? In the Middle Ages? In the Stone Age? Who knows, and the spirits are no help either. Their sense of time is so different that it\u2019s impossible to translate into human reckoning.\u201d It\u2019s the same issue the corebook had. Oral history is undervalued again, the context of modern human society gets ignored etc., etc. It\u2019s still a bad explanation and it still doesn\u2019t make sense. It\u2019s even worse here in trying to double down. Somebody was honestly okay with putting the notion in this book that the 80s and 90s are \u201cancient history\u201d. Come on!<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a nice little sidebar that offers better options for playing more experienced starting characters which is a good addition. It distinguishes between Cliath, Fostern and Adrath\u2026 which are terms borrowed from legacy-material that have never been explained in W5 before (because Ranks were removed). Somebody probably just assumed that these are still established terms in W5\u2026<br /> <br /> Then you get some more setting-information that\u2019s rather bland as well as a list of howls and Sept positions which are copy-pastes from the W20 corebook. It\u2019s not a straight up copy-past but you can clearly see how somebody looked at the W20 corebook and tried to present the same descriptions with different words.<br /> <br /> The Among Humans sections introduces Gaian Cults and honestly, I felt a bit underwhelmed. There\u2019s nothing substantial to this idea. The idea is that these are either humans who work together with Garou that don\u2019t care about the Veil or people who experienced Delirium but interpreted it as a moment of religious revelation. Their brush with the supernatural turns them into believers of some kind. And that\u2019s pretty much it. Like I said, underwhelming.<br /> <br /> Now we get to the characters portion and I can once again talk about how I don\u2019t like most of them. The biggest mistake this chapter has made is to make a human-born Silver Fang Ragabash named Dominique \u201cDeath-in-Word\u201d Omar the main-voice in this chapter. That guy is such an asshole!<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s part of the first quote you get from him:<br /> You know what I find annoying about being Garou? All the sincerity. It\u2019s really the worst. I was at a moot with that Gaia First girl, Aino, you know, the one who\u2019s suddenly become all the rage. I fail to see why. She kept berating us about working with humans to help Gaia, fighting the war on all fronts, equally in the Umbra, on the battlefield, in human politics, and in people\u2019s minds. She was pleading!<br /> It was terrible. I mean, sure. I believe all those things, too. But why does she have to be so strident about it! It\u2019s a moot \u2013 there\u2019s a lot to put up with already. Red Talons stinking of wet fur. Bone Gnawers hitting me up for charity. Some godawful Children of Gaia striking up one of their hippie songs.<br /> Wake up, the Sixties ended over fifty years ago! We\u2019re all about the end times now, the planet and it\u2019s destruction.<br /> <br /> Very unlikeable character but you get this section with quotes from characters about the fall of the Garou Nation. And it\u2019s this paradox I mentioned at the beginning: Everybody wants something like the Garou Nation \u2013 and everybody hated the Garou Nation when it was still around. But the kicker is that you get a taste at the end of how Jonas Albrecht is written in this book. This is how his quote starts: \u201cWe don't understand what we lost. My beautiful, perfect realm! The Garou Nation, the home for all of our kind.\u201d I don\u2019t know about you but the Jonas Albrecht that I knew from the legacy material would never exclaim \u201cMy beautiful, perfect realm!\u201d. Urgh, like nails on a chalkboard. Even if you were to say that this is a different Jonas Albrecht and not the legacy-one, it still is such a sad sap of a character in how this book depicts him. It\u2019s hard to believe that this character ever managed to be the king of the Garou Nation to begin with.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the Touchstones-section which we already saw in the previews (not anything more to it than what was shown in the previews) which then goes to the example Garou:<ul><li>Little Sister: Children of Gaia pacifist. That\u2019s it. Nothing more to it than that.</li> <li>Ilona and Karola Kor\u00e1nyi: Shadow Lord Ahroun, hate Silver Fangs, part of some evil baron\u2019s scheme, good Ahrouns.</li> <li>Dominique \u201cDeath-In-Word\u201d Omar: Ragabash who was recruited by the Silver Fangs mostly because he\u2019s wealthy. He fell in love with his role as a Ragabash. Translation: He\u2019s an asshole who takes his Ragabash-duties way too far.</li> <li>Shiro: A Hart Warden. Also a Galliard. And I bet you won\u2019t expect what comes next: He\u2019s a musician! Sigh</li> <li>Low Growl: Young wolfborn Silent Strider Philodox who travels from Sept to Sept helping human-born Garou to get more in touch with their wolf-nature.</li> </ul><br /> The Building A Social Environment section is useful as it talks about scale and in particular presenting the number of Garou in the setting as four different levels you should choose between: Non-existent \u2013 There\u2019s the PC-Pack and a few other Garou; Small \u2013 There\u2019s the PC-Pack, a small Sept with various Garou Elders and a rival Pack; Regional \u2013 There\u2019s a Sept with four or five Packs; The Nation In Ruins \u2013 The story involves multiple Septs with each having multiple Packs. The section would\u2019ve been even more interesting if there had been some commentary on why so much of the previous W5 stuff operated on the \u201cNon-existent\u201d-scale-level. Because I\u2019m curious if the \u201cnon-existent\u201d-scale is supposed to be the standard according to the current writing-team. Or maybe after the release of this book, they will embrace the bigger Regional and Nation In Ruins scale\u2026? I guess, we\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> Next you got a list of example Septs:<ul><li>Sept of the Moon\u2019s Blessing: A rolemodel for a good Sept, I guess. Not that interesting.</li> <li>Sept of the Water\u2019s Birth: Garou Sept attached to a human activist cause. Not sure what exactly the Garou are supposed to be doing here. It\u2019s a human activist cause. It doesn\u2019t really involve Garou-issues or -goals or needs the support of Garou-powers. The only thing I could picture here is doing either one of the two stereotypical W5 stories: Cult of Fenris needs to be stopped or you take the opposition to the activist cause and say \u201cOh, by the way, they\u2019re Fomori.\u201d.</li> <li>Sept of the North County: This is Jonas Albrecht\u2019s Sept where he lingers these days as this broken figure who has fallen to Harano. Besides getting Jonas out of Harano, the other story-hook is that he has adopted this Lebanese teenager from New York. He has given her a new name (which is weird) and she\u2019s now called Mari (after one of Jonas\u2019 Packmates). Also, she\u2019s supposed to be his successor. And it suggests you could play this out by having one player play \u201cPrincess Mari\u201d and have the other players be her \u201chonor guard\u201d as Mari is chasing her destiny of being the next leader of the Garou Nation.</li> <li>Sept of the Bitter Frost: A Cult of Fenris Sept that is very welcoming and open-minded when outsiders are around and tries to get newcomers to join the Sept. But then behind closed doors the Cult show what they\u2019re truly like and abuse/torture the newcomers until they join the Cult or they become a human sacrifice instead.</li> </ul><br /> There\u2019s a new element introduced towards the end of this chapter called \u201cGreat Hunts\u201d which is the term for any effort that involves multiple Septs to work together to achieve. I don\u2019t know but the first time I heard this it reminded me of Werewolf: The Forsaken. \u201cGreat Hunt\u201d just doesn\u2019t quite feel right for what Garou would call this, I feel like. The section also lists \u201cGreat Hunts of the past\u201d and it\u2019s essentially just a long list of references to legacy-material. The only present-day newish Great Hunt that is mentioned is called \u201cThe Breath of Gaia\u201d and it\u2019s targeting the southern states of the US and the Mediterranean in Europe. It goes after places \u201cwhere cheap, exploited labor is used in industrial farming, meatpacking plants, heavy industry and other sectors with a significant negative impact on both the environment and human communities.\u201d Again, another thing where this just feels overly broad and vague. And it lacks Garou-specific flavor.<br /> <br /> Oh, and another famous Great Hunt is called \u201cThe Dead Purge\u201d which starts like this: \u201cMost Garou consider vampires to be servants of the Wyrm and agents of the enemy. While suspicion and hatred of the undead have always been part of Garou culture, it has escalated greatly in the last 10 years.\u201d This gets continued in Chapter Five where vampires are discussed again but you read right, this book brings back the idea that most Garou think vampires are servants of the Wyrm and that they have an inherently antagonistic relationship with them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Chapter Three: Rites of the Moon</span><br /> <br /> Honestly it\u2019s exactly what you\u2019d expect: A list of new Rites you can use in your game. One that\u2019s particularly interesting is the Rite of Renunciation as it\u2019s the process of leaving your Tribe. But more than that, it introduces the concept of \u201cForsworn\u201d (aka the Ronin from legacy-material) in a sidebar. Tribe-less Garou are a thing again.<br /> <br /> This chapter also offers a list of story-hooks but none of them seem that interesting in how bland and obvious they are. I bet most STs would be capable of coming up with stuff like this on their own. There\u2019s nothing particularly insightful or Garou-specific offered here.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Chapter Four: Saga of the Wolf</span><br /> <br /> This chapter is dedicated to Moots and it brings nothing new to the table. It essentially just re-introduces the W5 audience to the particulars of how a Moot works. And the examples are again a bit on the blander side of things. Again, I imagine that most STs could come up with these broad story-hooks on their own.<br /> <br /> Where the chapter gets interesting, though, is towards the end where \u201cLegendary Rites\u201d are discussed. These are reenactments of critical events in Garou history. The way it\u2019s presented it comes off like an idea that obviously came from someone with a LARP-background and I do wonder how well this concept would even work if the players aren\u2019t game for this bit of a high-concept-idea of playing characters who play other characters in this reenactment. Four examples are presented (Ross the She-Wolf Fights Union Bromide, The Tale of the Storm-Eater, The Quest for the Silver Crown, The Last Battle).<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s look at \u201cThe Quest for the Silver Crown\u201d. You have a Dramatis Personae where roles get distributed. This particular Legendary Rite calls for five main-roles and two groups of people being side-characters. Again, let\u2019s just say that this feels very much like a LARP-thing.<br /> <br /> And then you get a sequence of scenes that look like this:<br /> <br /> 1. The Attack: Black Spiral Dancers attack Queen Morningkill and Albrecht\u2019s packmates. The battle ends with the death of Morningkill and the attackers fleeing. (This battle, like all the battles in this Legendary Rite, should be roleplayed with regular combat rules.)<br /> 2. The King: Lord Arkady and Jonas Albrecht arrive at the murder scene, and Arkady proclaims himself king. Jonas Albrecht disputes this and takes his pack to look for the Silver Crown.<br /> 3. The Search: Jonas Albrecht and his pack look for the crown everywhere but do not find it. (The characters should describe where in the world they go to look for the talisman. The pyramids? The rainforest? The North Pole? Rolls of Wits + Survival should be made, and on a result of two or fewer successes, characters take 2 Superficial Physical damage.)<br /> 4. The Ambush: Black Spiral Dancers ambush the pack. Another combat ensues. (The Black Spiral Dancers get to start with surprise attacks.)<br /> <br /> And this goes up to 11. Also, everybody mentioned here are supposed to be Garou playing these roles (including the Black Spiral Dancers). It also is expected that these scenes are acted out. What is part of this concept is that the events aren\u2019t fixed. So in this particular case you have divergent routes where Albrecht\u2019s pack either gets captured or they win against the Black Spiral Dancers and get them to lead to Dagrack, the main-BSD-guy. And it can end in different ways, too. There\u2019s one ending where Albrecht wins the day and there\u2019s another ending where Arkady becomes the next king of the Garou Nation by defeating Albrecht.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of this but I can\u2019t help but feel that this one\u2019s solely for LARP-play. It\u2019s hard to imagine how this would go well at the table.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Chapter Five: Speaking With The Enemy</span><br /> <br /> As mentioned at the start, this chapter is a revision of the Allies/Antagonist-chapter from the W5 corebook. All the factions are re-examined under the auspice of under what circumstances an alliance might be possible. But as mentioned categories like vampires aren\u2019t in this neutral zone like it was sometimes described during the release of the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> This is the best chapter of the book, though, as it provides much better write-ups for the Cult of Fenris, Stargazers and pretty much all the categories of allies and antagonists. The book also adds Bear-Shifters and Rat-Shifters. It still doesn\u2019t come close to the depth these shifters got in the legacy-material but for example, it\u2019s heavily implied that the Bear-Shifters are still the same-old Gurahl from previous editions.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s one exception, though, which are the Black Spiral Dancers. It\u2019s different from the W5 corebook and personally I never ran BSD like how it\u2019s described here. First, it\u2019s stated that while the Fenrir are a Tribe fallen to Hauglosk, the BSD are a Tribe fallen to Harano. It says: \u201cSome, inspired by how the Cult of Fenris rose into prominence, propose that the Black Spiral Dancers are a tribe in harano, albeit a kind that inverted the tribe\u2019s fighting spirit as opposed to destroying it.\u201d<br /> <br /> But this is a much more morally gray version of the BSD. This version of the BSD is still very much invested in their White Howler heritage and is still interested in stuff like honoring pacts the White Howlers made in the past (one story-hook that\u2019s suggested in the book is that a BSD-pack might show up to an abandoned caern that the PCs are also targeting but the BSD-pack say it\u2019s their right to claim it because it used to belong to the White Howlers). Also, the text describes how the BSD don\u2019t want to get pushed around by Fomori and/or Pentex and if they feel slighted, they are willing to help Garou in order to teach their erstwhile allies a lesson. I always portrayed BSD as much more monstrous and psychopathic so the version described in this book is a bit different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Appendix: Systems</span><br /> <br /> Here you get new Merits and Flaws\u2026 Nothing noteworthy here. The one, though, that absolutely doesn\u2019t work is the two-dot Flaw \u201cAdditional Ban\u201d. It does what it says: Your character gets an additional Ban from another Tribe. Why? Who knows\u2026 Similarly to this version of the Flaw from the V5 Players Guide it comes with the lazy addendum saying \u201cThe Storyteller can prohibit this Flaw if the second Ban would cause problems for, or lack impact in, the chronicle.\u201d If you think, it could cause problems or lack impact, just don\u2019t put it in the book! Or at least put in the work of listing what combinations of Bans are good-to-go.<br /> <br /> The book adds one new Native Gift. Yep, just one. And it isn\u2019t a particularly good one as well. It\u2019s called The Howl Carries and it does this: \u201cThe Garou steels themselves and howl loudly. That howl is picked up and repeated by mundane wolves who travel some distance and then repeat the howl until the sun next rises or sets. Any Garou within a few miles recognizes the howl as unusual (including Garou unknown to the howler), as do some spirits. Humans, however, have no chance of intercepting the message.\u201d So it\u2019s a howl-power that\u2019s reliant on mundane wolves\u2026 I would love to talk to whoever wrote this and direct them to pg 74 of a book called Shattered Nation which introduces this Rite called \u201cRite of the Borne Word\u201d where you task a spirit with delivering a spoken message to a specific target. Yep, this very book has a Rite that does the same thing this Gift does \u2013 but better.<br /> <br /> Also\u2026 in contrast to the book I can think of a few ways humans might be able to intercept a howl that\u2019s carried by mundane wolves\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Appendix: Loresheets</span><br /> <br /> There\u2019s something odd about these Loresheets. All seven of them are centered on one particular Garou. But what makes it odd that in all seven cases something very different is going on when you delve into the dot-ratings. Despite the names always being one particular Garou no Loresheet is actually about you being a close contact of this one Garou and that person giving your character stuff. So I will always first explain who the showcased Garou is and then I will explain what\u2019s going on with the dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Aino \u201cLil Gaia\u201d Mets\u00e4l\u00e4:</b><ul><li>A Red Talon Ragabash who\u2019s a Finnish activist and clearly inspired by Greta Thunberg. She has an NGO called \u201cGaia First\u201d that \u201corganize demonstrations, civil disobedience, and social media campaigns to inform the populace and to demand that governments and corporations act according to their aims\u201d. Her detractors also accuse her of being a Stolen Moon.</li> <li>What the dots describe is you becoming a member of \u201cGaia First\u201d and gradually getting more access to that organization which can get you local intel, allies, safe houses and they\u2019ll create demonstrations, civil unrest and whatnot on your behalf at higher ratings.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Alejandro \u201cVaporfang\u201d Mendoza:</b><ul><li>A Bone Gnawer Galliard who\u2019s a world-famous hacker who\u2019s getting into secret databases from governments, corporations and rich oligarchs in order to leak those secrets to the public. This character is clearly inspired by Edward Snowden.</li> <li>What makes this character odd, though, is the description notes that he\u2019s currently in prison. So\u2026 how exactly would PCs come into contact with him\u2026? Sure, I could envision scenarios to make this work but here\u2019s a quicker solution: Just don\u2019t make your Loresheet about a character in prison!</li> <li>The Loresheet notes that you need at least two dots in Technology and that has something to do with what\u2019s actually going on in the dots. As you gain dots, you actually become proficient in doing the same thing that Vaporfang is famous for.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Jonas Albrecht:</b><ul><li>Pretty self-explanatory who he is.</li> <li>What\u2019s going on in the dots is that as you gain more, you become a more ardent follower of Jonas Albrecht and a firm believer in restoring the Garou Nation. The mechanics are pretty interesting here as you gain bonus-dice from defending the ideals of the Garou Nation but also you can get further bonus-dice by taking dots of Harano (and later Hauglosk as well). And it all starts with the first dot being that once per session you can add your Harano-score to your dice-pool. You essentially play a zealot who\u2019s burning themselves out in pursuit of rebuilding the Garou Nation.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Liu \u201cReturning Maiden\u201d Aihan:</b><ul><li>She grew up in Shanghai and is a taikonaut who had her First Change in space (which is a bit hard to believe). But the actual focus is that as she had her First Change in space she has no Auspice. She\u2019s a mysterious figure because instead it seems like she\u2019s all five Auspices at the same time. She\u2019s supposed to be a Galestalker according to some but the way she\u2019s acting makes a lot of Garou think that she\u2019s a Stargazer instead.</li> <li>The dots are about your character becoming a moon cultist and getting closer to Luna. First dot is about you being able to learn Gifts from other Auspices. Second Dot is about you being able to switch Auspices for the purpose of Rites and other ceremonial purposes. Third Dot gives you bonus die when interacting with Lunes and other spirits of Luna. Fourth dot allows you once per session to treat an attack with silver as superficial damage. And fifth dot\u2026 * drumroll * Moon-Path (aka Moon-Bridge). Yep, they\u2019re back \u2013 sort-of. This fifth dot allows the character to create moon-bridges between two caerns.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Oba \u201cTrailblazer\u201d Makinde:</b><ul><li>A Glass Walker Theurge who\u2019s an entrepeneuer and CEO of a surveillance-company called Omniscent. Here\u2019s the thing about Omniscent: It\u2019s a Pentex-front. And Trailblazer knows this. He often comes in conflict with other Garou (especially the aforementioned Lil Gaia and her \u201cGaia First\u201d-organization) because his grand plan is to take out Pentex from within.</li> <li>The dots describe the PC rising in the ranks of Omniscent and giving them access to information about what Pentex and the various corporations connected to it are up to. And you get dots in Resources.</li> <li>It gets weirder towards the higher end as you get permanent dot of Harano or Hauglosk at four dots and at five dots it says: \u201cYou gain a level of Aggravated Willpower damage if you attempt to harm Omniscent, Trailblazer, or any of their business partners, including Pentex and its fronts.\u201d That certainly makes it seem like that whole \u201ctaking Pentex down from within\u201d doesn\u2019t quite work how it\u2019s pitched by Trailblazer\u2026</li> </ul><br /> <b>Ross the She-Wolf Jackson:</b><ul><li>A Silent Strider Philodox and a proud gay man (I mention that because that\u2019s what the Loresheet is about). He\u2019s an environmental activist who has earned quite a bit of Renown fighting Union Bromide in Nagpur.</li> <li>It\u2019s a bit hard to pin down what exactly is going on here except that LGBTQ+, pollution and minority-groups are the focus\u2026 sort-of. First dot allows you to have a sixth sense for knowing when environmental pollution is occurring and how bad it is. Second dot gives you a bonus-die for the first action after you have shape-shifted. Third dot gives you a four-dice-bonus once per session if you\u2019re trying to prevent environmental pollution. Fourth dot allows your character to change their sex every time they shapeshift (at the cost of a point of Willpower and an additional Rage-check). Fifth dot says this: \u201cYou are a member of a minority group. Once per story, If you spend a scene hanging out with members of this community, you recover all lost Willpower. As with Ross, you are expected to help and protect this group, and if you ever refuse a call for help from someone in this minority you sustain three points of Aggravated Willpower damage and lose this trait until you have provided said help.\u201d I guess, this whole Loresheet works best if you\u2019re part of a minority group from the very beginning and that\u2019s what gets you to this Loresheet.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Vandana \u201cThe Impresario\u201d Puri:</b><ul><li>A Hart Warden Galliard that\u2019s well known for organizing Moots and Rites (like a Rite of Passage). She\u2019s also very invested in hunting down Stolen Moons.</li> <li>The dots in this case are nother example like Vaporblade where you essentially turn into a copy of this character and become proficient in what this character is famous for. You\u2019re getting better at organizing events and you\u2019re getting better at tracking down Stolen Moons and killing them.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Conclusion:</span><br /> <br /> After going through the whole book, I think the thing that stuck most with me is how much of this book is just about bringing back legacy-material. Meanwhile, newer concepts that are W5-specific like Moon and Gaian Cults don\u2019t get nearly enough coverage in this book. Rather, in contrast to the \u201cre-imagination, not continuation\u201d-slogan from the W5 corebook, this is a book that quite earnestly invested in being a continuation.<br /> <br /> On one hand, I think W5 is richer for having all these bits and pieces from the legacy-material back in the W5-setting. On the other hand, though, this book hasn\u2019t managed to move past any of the big issues the W5 corebook had. Does the fall of the Garou Nation make any more sense now? Not really. Has the negative attitude towards oral history and this \u201cWho knows\u201d-attitude been addressed? No, instead it just doubled down and it still just sounds as absurd as when it came up in the W5 corebook. Does it offer an alternative route for Garou to aspire to? No, it just feels like everyone wants to bring the Garou Nation back with these ephemeral caveats that this time it will be completely different and much better. And it would\u2019ve been things like the Moon and Gaian Cults (the idea of lifting the Veil and working more closely together with humans) which are actual genuine alternative visions. So it\u2019s sad that it\u2019s exactly in those areas where you don\u2019t get enough information.<br /> <br /> And then I gotta wonder: Especially if you\u2019re familiar with the legacy-material\u2026 what does this book actually add to the game? All the people who went online and asked about more information for moots, for example. Often in situations like that, they were told to go look up the older books for more information. So they did that. And this book is essentially the official equivalent of just that. The people who wrote those sections also just went back to the older books and gave you that same information. So how much is this book truly offering to its readers\u2026?<br /> <br /> I think, the parts on Pack-Types and all the sections that had more of a toolbox-approach are worthy additions, though. Getting STs to consider the number of Garou in the setting and discussing the options or helping with session zero by giving general overviews in what terms you can define Packs. And personally, instead of spending all that wordcount on painstakingly writing back in all the legacy-material, I think everybody would just be happier by going for a toolbox-approach and letting everybody play the way they want. You want your legacy-stuff back, your 30-Garou Septs and epic adventures? Sure. You want your Age of Apocalypse, fallen Garou Nation and the setting consists of the PC Pack and only one or two other Garou? That\u2019s fine as well. And for example, if you just focus on making Moon Cults a genuinely interesting thing, I\u2019m sure there will be W20 groups who will try to bring that into their game. In the same way that there should be no hard feelings about anyone who likes a part of the legacy-material and wants to bring those into a W5 game.<br /> <br /> It all comes back to the W5 corebook. That\u2019s one of the bigger issues W5 has. In trying to re-examine core-concepts from this book, they just came off as even more absurd. Like the fallen Garou Nation. It fell apart because Garou couldn\u2019t work together but if you have these Septs who have these grievances and who won\u2019t work together, then in the face of the Apocalypse and the war against the Wyrm, naturally you would wanna make it your goal to get them to work together. But the whole point of the fall of the Garou Nation is that these Garou couldn\u2019t work together. So you need to introduce a reason for why this time around would be different. But you\u2019re making the change too radical and you\u2019re not playing WtA anymore. On the other hand, you don\u2019t do that and you\u2019d wonder why the story wouldn\u2019t be just about history repeating itself. These issues are so fundamental that you would\u2019ve needed here a different approach with different ideas from the very beginning. But instead with W5 you\u2019ll just run into these contradictions again and again.<br /> <br /> All in all, as a book it\u2019s a good addition but it can\u2019t move beyond the shortcomings of this game\u2019s setting. The only good sign here is that each future supplement that is similar to this one will be W5 getting one inch further away from the problems of the corebook.<br /> <br /> Oh and hopefully, we\u2019ll get better in-character-writing in the future\u2026<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T09:13:13-07:00","id":1541232,"title":"","content":"Aino &quot;Pikku Maaemo&quot; Mets\u00e4l\u00e4 annoys me. Not just because of her nationality, but the loresheet is basically focused not on the group's impact but how it benefits the character. Also Death-in-Words hits the flaw in her depiction accidentally on the head; Trying and caring are for losers.<br /> <br /> I need to read more on the BSDs, but if you look at the Stargazer section, it basically outlines the ideal garou the core wanted; Someone trying other methods to heal Gaia than violence. But they, somehow, are not playable for artificial reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T09:31:29-07:00","id":1541233,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this Gaia First organization in the way it's portrayed with the dot-ratings reminded me more of a global conspiracy than an actual activist movement. That Loresheet certainly veers in the direction of going all-in on that &quot;Garou as activists&quot;-idea that I still don't really like. Because what are Garou as violent half-spirit killing-machines supposed to add to a purely mundane human activist cause? You're not gonna push through an election reform or something by shifting into your Crinos Form.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I liked the Stargazer section more than the corebook-one but that section once again focuses more on the &quot;fight smarter, not harder&quot;-aspect which is something all Garou in W5 should aspire to. Rather, what W5 should do since they want them to be these mysterious non-playable &quot;allies&quot; is to emphasize their enigmatic behavior, I think. Like, a Stargazer comes around and tells you the way to get a Pentex-Front to go bankrupt is to do ridiculous stuff like eating noodles at a bus-stop every day at a certain time and buying specific flowers from a shop. Stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T09:47:47-07:00","id":1541234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541233#post1541233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this Gaia First organization in the way it's portrayed with the dot-ratings reminded me more of a global conspiracy than an actual activist movement. That Loresheet certainly veers in the direction of going all-in on that &quot;Garou as activists&quot;-idea that I still don't really like. Because what are Garou as violent half-spirit killing-machines supposed to add to a purely mundane human activist cause? You're not gonna push through an election reform or something by shifting into your Crinos Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, because the point of that loresheet seems to be to say that the efforts of those passionate don't do anything. That it is all just what use is the movement to -you-, not what it can -do.- Notice how not once does the loresheet mention the effect on nature or policy the group has. It is purely in how much shit the PC can get or get away with.<br /> <br /> And I mean, you get minus dice for eating processed food. If that doesn't tell you the wanted message, I don't know what will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541233#post1541233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I liked the Stargazer section more than the corebook-one but that section once again focuses more on the &quot;fight smarter, not harder&quot;-aspect which is something all Garou in W5 should aspire to. Rather, what W5 should do since they want them to be these mysterious non-playable &quot;allies&quot; is to emphasize their enigmatic behavior, I think. Like, a Stargazer comes around and tells you the way to get a Pentex-Front to go bankrupt is to do ridiculous stuff like eating noodles at a bus-stop every day at a certain time and buying specific flowers from a shop. Stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it is written, which is so artificial it stinks of bleach, the Gazers would be ALL for telling other garou their methods. But they won't listen.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T15:32:23-07:00","id":1541248,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t really follow or play 5th edition much so I appreciate threads like this and I\u2019ll talk about some of the things you mentioned and how I might consider cribbing them for previous editions if that interests folks<br /> <br /> <b>Introduction</b><br /> <br /> \u2022In theory I do like the idea of using a sort of vulgar, abrasive, \u2018dirty realism\u2019 tone for Garou and Garou society but this is clearly a case of YMMV depending on taste and how well its done. I do think it can be a good fit when done well in both how it serves the (imperfect term) \u2018savage horror\u2019 element of the game and the aspect of the werewolf that\u2019s essentially a frenzied murderer as well as the contrast that this tone can strike with the more pulpy Conan/Robert Howard elements of pageantry which Garou culture can also use<br /> <br /> \u2022While such a tone has use throughout I think it would be particularly useful for young turks and outsiders within the Nation as well as groups like the Bone Gnawers in general, who might talk like a Chuck Palahniuk or Charles Bukowski character<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1</b><br /> <br /> \u2022I like the pack dynamic dials for interpersonal relationship, spiritual relationship, &amp; relationship with the veil although perhaps spiritual relationship could use further differentiation - the options mentioned sound kind of samey. The books have always played with the idea that some Garou are hostile and coercive with spirits while others are reverent and conciliatory (and others are in between) and that might have been an interesting dynamic to spotlight there<br /> <br /> \u2022I like the idea of pack-types and even the pack-systems mentioned but they could probably be tweaked somewhat. I do like Territory having to do with the health of the territory and familiarity with it but it could also have certain tags, maybe something like the stuff in WtF. I like Community too and it would be interesting to distinguish between human, kinfolk, &amp; wolf/wild community relations. Spirit feels a little weird. Perhaps one could argue that the umbra of a pack\u2019s protectorate ought to fit under Territory but even so Spirit feels like it ought to reflect a familiarity with the prevalent and important spirit\u2019s of a pack\u2019s protectorate and the pack\u2019s relationship with them. I like the concepts here but they could use a few tweaks maybe<br /> <br /> \u2022I like the concept of pack types and it can be useful to have lists like these for inspiration and an exploration of archetypes and dynamics<br /> <br /> \u2022The Moon Cults idea is very cool imo and something is definitely be interested in. Garou society already functions as a nested network of cults to begin with and it could be a very rich vein to more thoroughly explore. I wish they\u2019d offered a more concrete explanation of what the Moon Cults in general are like but still, credit where it\u2019s due<br /> <br /> \u2022I like the idea of Pack Actions but it sounds like this section really went off the rails. This is where something like Blades in the Dark or related games could offer inspiration, because I do like the general concept of systems for pack-actions and their effects in play, but they would definitely need to be more archetypal and flexible rather then specific. Reconnoiter &amp; Ambush both work fine but some of these are def too specific. Off the top of my head I\u2019d say that Reconnoiter (gather information), Ambush, Hunt (WtF style chasing down a target), Patrol (surveying a territory or keeping certain territory routines upkept), Sabotage, Assault, Ritual, Howl, etc. would be more in line with what I\u2019d be looking for in general systems for pack-actions<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 2</b><br /> <br /> \u2022I feel like there\u2019s a current of something in the idea of Generations as described and how most active Garou (like PCs) tend to live in the present but like others I disagree with its framing within the context of W5. Still, I do think there\u2019s a nugget there, about how many Garou are like your pack of young PCs and are mostly concerned with the hectic, breakneck speed of Garou war life, and will be lucky to survive a decade of it. What I feel W5 leaves out though and what legacy can help with, particularly 1e/2e is the idea that the pedal-to-the-medal image of Garou was never the whole of the nation but rather its cadres of relatively young packs. The Garou nation in legacy also had Old Wolves (retired Garou who had yet to feel the need to go out Winter Wolf-style and stayed around to teach the young, be the audience at moots &amp; help establish renown, teach rites, etc; generally being the crabby chorus that both criticize and guide the PCs), Guardians of the Nation (the workhorse Garou who were either sitting on their laurels with a steady position within a step providing local leadership or the Garou who preferred to dedicate their energy to Sept maintaince instead of roving around anruth style in search of adventure and Wyrms to slay), &amp; Drop Outs (Garou who did not spend the majority of their time working for the Nation, whether at Sept or as Anruth, and instead did whatever else held their fancy but could possibly be called upon as allies for more active Garou), etc. <br /> -Plus the whole attitude towards oral tradition isn\u2019t a great look for W5 and while I can buy that Garou would tailor stories to fit the audience of every generation I don\u2019t buy that there wouldn\u2019t be competing cliques of both elders and spirits who kept alive certain versions of important historical narratives<br /> <br /> \u2022I like the idea of Garou &amp; Gaian cults<br /> <br /> \u2022NPCs seem underwhelming; I like some good metaplot writing as an option/sideshow but this doesn\u2019t seem to be it. Potential in some of them though <br /> <br /> \u2022The Albrecht stuff is rough. I could buy some version of this concept in the right chronicle - a sort of quasi-apocalypse scenario where most Garou think they\u2019ve failed to stop the Apocalypse and it\u2019s too late to do anything and Jonas ends up as a washed-up could-have-been wallowing in angst and despairing for the world he lost and for what could have been, but it doesn\u2019t really feel earned given the context of W5. This just feels kind of like they turned Albrecht into an updated Jacob Morningkill, not really into it <br /> <br /> \u2022I like the idea for more Sept building tools although I don\u2019t know how useful these would be for me given their specifically W5 context <br /> <br /> \u2022I like the idea of Great Hunts, although maybe they could have a different name but I think Great Hunt works fine, and it would be interesting to think what sort of Infrastructure/Conspiracy level activity (to crib from Chronicles a bit) that Garou would get up to<br /> <br /> \u2022The Cult Sept sounds like the most interesting one to me tbh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T16:37:01-07:00","id":1541252,"title":"","content":"I can't believe you already got through all of that. Kudos, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> <br /> <br /> My first look was into the Stargazers, and I'm fascinated how they're essentially Garou that want non-violent solutions to the Wyrm, and it's not that they are mysterious and unknown, it's that the horrible, horrible Garou of W5 just don't want to listen to them. This feels like quite a lost opportunity, especially combined with the sidebar that the Garou don't differentiate the Moon Cults from the Stargazers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T19:44:28-07:00","id":1541256,"title":"","content":"Exactly how are you supposed to come up with a non-violent solution to the Wyrm? It's always been clear that the ultimate solution to one third of reality going corrupt can't be &quot;fight Banes for eternity&quot; and that you can't just fight a head-on war against all of human society but it's also been clear that sometimes you have to sabotage a mining project or fight some Banes due to lack of other options. And on the scale that W5 is supposed to operate, &quot;heal the Wyrm's madness&quot; isn't an option anyway.<br /> <br /> So, what are the Stargazers actually <i>doing</i> that is materially different from what the other Garou are doing? What's their track record of success compared to everyone else's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T20:09:46-07:00","id":1541257,"title":"","content":"They brought Arkady back just to rehash the same plot from end 2e? This really is obsessed with re-treading everything leading up to and including Revised. At this rate, maybe we'll get back up to W20's level of forward thinking by 2030.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T20:39:23-07:00","id":1541261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541257#post1541257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They brought Arkady back just to rehash the same plot from end 2e? This really is obsessed with re-treading everything leading up to and including Revised. At this rate, maybe we'll get back up to W20's level of forward thinking by 2030.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Albrecht currently playing the part of Morningkill....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T20:50:58-07:00","id":1541263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541261#post1541261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Albrecht currently playing the part of Morningkill....</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrift, dear Horatio, thrift. The same character can be made a player for both parts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T23:13:53-07:00","id":1541266,"title":"","content":"I'm a w5 enjoyer. I'm enjoying my long campaign.<br /> I like this game as a third game about werewolves.<br /> <br /> This is my opinion: this book is utter garbage.<br /> It actually betrays even the premises of w5 core book. The npc are a bunch of complainers and they are presented as more human than human. Exactly the opposite of the game premise of &quot;wrong answers for the right problem&quot; or &quot;behead those motherfuckers who are exploiting the earth&quot;. Vaguely very human characters with no true solutions or just inspired by real life people. This books looks like a bad way to go back to some legacy content, and it does it in the worst way possible. Albrecht is a joke. Elders did that, Elders ruined this, Elders wronged those. The werewolf society is very authoritarian. Now suddenly, Elders are afraid to give orders or to do something &quot;&quot;because of fear to lose power or retaliation&quot;&quot;. The new hope are the young ones: all the solutions proposed in this book are extremely fucking human. Rage is not even mentioned. The tragedy of being a rampaging monster is absent. They even massacrated our buddies, Konietzsko and Tvarivich. They want the Cult of fenris as the big bad but what they describe looks like standard get of fenris from 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> I may say that I like great hunts, a bunch of mechanics, and even the rough way the garou talk between them, but at its core to me it looks like an extremely bad way to trying to appeal older players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 08-31-2024, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T23:47:50-07:00","id":1541269,"title":"","content":"Looking at the BSD example story ideas and comparing them to the CoF story ideas really tells you who they want as the main bad guy. BSD ones are almost all about redeeming those of the Wyrm with only one treating them as foes. While all CoF ones are treating them as something you cannot trust EVER and attack Gaians willy nilly.<br /> <br /> Even though CoF are still on Gaia's side and BSDs very much are not.<br /> <br /> Nevermind the Stargazers still being willing to help but the book itself doesn't let them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T04:38:53-07:00","id":1541282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541233#post1541233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this Gaia First organization in the way it's portrayed with the dot-ratings reminded me more of a global conspiracy than an actual activist movement. That Loresheet certainly veers in the direction of going all-in on that &quot;Garou as activists&quot;-idea that I still don't really like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean WtE author did actually play around with the idea of garou as activists with the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound </a>where the tribe actually have it's start as an activist org around the Vietnam war. Of course the issues that Hearthbound are advocate for (Mainly the rights of kinfolk and Warborn) are unique to garou and they will use force if needed since in lore they did crush a major moot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-31-2024, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T05:50:05-07:00","id":1541283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541282#post1541282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean WtE author did actually play around with the idea of garou as activists with the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound </a>where the tribe actually have it's start as an activist org around the Vietnam war. Of course the issues that Hearthbound are advocate for (Mainly the rights of kinfolk and Warborn) are unique to garou and they will use if needed since in lore they did crush a major moot.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the main-problem with a lot of this where they try to introduce real-world issues (like with the Sept in Italy and the Libyan refugees). You have to put in some effort, do some worldbuilding and try to find an angle to make it fit within Garou-society and/or the animistic worldview of WtA. Even with something like environmentalism... It's not like you can just point at a generic werewolf and say &quot;Obviously werewolves are connected to environmentalist activism.&quot;. The reason this matters in WtA is because of the animistic setting and how the specific werewolves in this setting worship Gaia. That's how you get to the environmentalist angle.<br /> <br /> Instead what happens in W5 is that these real-world-issues are just mentioned and get tossed around without considering how to introduce them into the WtA-setting. Why are the Garou involved in this? How are they connected to this activist-activity?<br /> <br /> For example, that Sept of the Water's Birth... This is how I would reframe it: The situation in Libya has only been getting worse and worse since Gaddafi was killed. More and more Fomori are popping up, working together and forming dangerous gangs. With every day the Wyrm's influence seems to be getting stronger. The Italian Sept has been contacted by Garou in Libya who are asking for help in taking in their Kin and younger Garou along with their most precious Talismans. But another nearby Sept led by the Cult of Fenris also heard of this plea for help and thinks these Garou are cowards. And the Sept of the Water's Birth are cowards too for considering to support this. If anything, they all should go over there instead and put things right! Some Garou in the Sept are grumbling as well that maybe the Fenrir are right. But helping the Garou, the Kin and their families together with bringing over the precious Talismans may not be as easy as expected as a new security-company has been hired to patrol the Mediterranean border. Troubling reports of excessive brutality, corruption and guards having strange tattoos and scars indicate that this new company may be a Pentex-front.<br /> <br /> The refugee-issue is still in there but now at least it's a WtA-story first and foremost. It's also striking how in both the case of this Sept and in the game Purgatory with this refugee-issue the perspective gets recentered on Europe. Because I thought this when I played Purgatory as well. Isn't the more interesting angle for WtA to make this about the Garou in a country like Libya or Afghanistan who are guarding a caern but due to circumstances beyond their control their human family, contacts or allies are planning to leave the country for Europe because things are so bad? The question of leaving and becoming a refugee has a very different calculus when you're a Garou. Rather than making it about activism in Europe, you make it about that. Because that's another thing that's striking about featured W5 locations is how most of them are in North America and Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T07:52:37-07:00","id":1541286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541283#post1541283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's the main-problem with a lot of this where they try to introduce real-world issues (like with the Sept in Italy and the Libyan refugees). You have to put in some effort, do some worldbuilding and try to find an angle to make it fit within Garou-society and/or the animistic worldview of WtA. Even with something like environmentalism... It's not like you can just point at a generic werewolf and say &quot;Obviously werewolves are connected to environmentalist activism.&quot;. The reason this matters in WtA is because of the animistic setting and how the specific werewolves in this setting worship Gaia. That's how you get to the environmentalist angle.<br /> <br /> Instead what happens in W5 is that these real-world-issues are just mentioned and get tossed around without considering how to introduce them into the WtA-setting. Why are the Garou involved in this? How are they connected to this activist-activity?<br /> <br /> For example, that Sept of the Water's Birth... This is how I would reframe it: The situation in Libya has only been getting worse and worse since Gaddafi was killed. More and more Fomori are popping up, working together and forming dangerous gangs. With every day the Wyrm's influence seems to be getting stronger. The Italian Sept has been contacted by Garou in Libya who are asking for help in taking in their Kin and younger Garou along with their most precious Talismans. But another nearby Sept led by the Cult of Fenris also heard of this plea for help and thinks these Garou are cowards. And the Sept of the Water's Birth are cowards too for considering to support this. If anything, they all should go over there instead and put things right! Some Garou in the Sept are grumbling as well that maybe the Fenrir are right. But helping the Garou, the Kin and their families together with bringing over the precious Talismans may not be as easy as expected as a new security-company has been hired to patrol the Mediterranean border. Troubling reports of excessive brutality, corruption and guards having strange tattoos and scars indicate that this new company may be a Pentex-front.<br /> <br /> The refugee-issue is still in there but now at least it's a WtA-story first and foremost. It's also striking how in both the case of this Sept and in the game Purgatory with this refugee-issue the perspective gets recentered on Europe. Because I thought this when I played Purgatory as well. Isn't the more interesting angle for WtA to make this about the Garou in a country like Libya or Afghanistan who are guarding a caern but due to circumstances beyond their control their human family, contacts or allies are planning to leave the country for Europe because things are so bad? The question of leaving and becoming a refugee has a very different calculus when you're a Garou. Rather than making it about activism in Europe, you make it about that. Because that's another thing that's striking about featured W5 locations is how most of them are in North America and Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sept of the Water's Birth, though, is told to be born explicitly out of Garou activists who are there for &quot;<i>the purpose of trying to keep people from dying in the sea; its members radicalized by the easy acceptance of death in the human society around them&quot;</i>. The two named characters of the Sept turned into Garou respectively because they witnessed the atrocities of the sea lanes and because they survived them.<br /> <br /> It's an example of a Sept who is tighly interwoven with human issues, while the other have varying degrees of relation with Mankind:<br /> <br /> -Strong relation with humans but also strong relations with Garou Society: Sept of the Moon's Blessing, who is into union organizing and preserving local traditions from the encroachment of big business but is also a meeting place for wandering packs and the one place where moots are called.<br /> <br /> -Low relation with humans but strong relations with Garou Society: Sept of the North Country, which is an isolated temple to Garou traditions and treasures, disconnected from every Weaver influence.<br /> <br /> -Low relations with humans but also low relations with Garou Society: Sept of the Bitter Frost, which is the classic isolated cult fortress where you arrive in joy and everything ends in horror.<br /> <br /> The 4 Septs show different sides of Garou Society and of its relations with nature and Humans, from the active hatred to the open mingling.<br /> <br /> Also, if one of the frequent complaints against W5 werewolves is that they are not heroes enough, getting involved against human trafficking only if there is some hint at a Pentex front ... well, they would be quite touchy heroes, to put it mildly, when confronted by one of the biggest tragedies of these recent times.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T08:53:07-07:00","id":1541290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541286#post1541286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sept of the Water's Birth, though, is told to be born explicitly out of Garou activists who are there for &quot;<i>the purpose of trying to keep people from dying in the sea; its members radicalized by the easy acceptance of death in the human society around them&quot;</i>. The two named characters of the Sept turned into Garou respectively because they witnessed the atrocities of the sea lanes and because they survived them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it doesn't work. This takes a real-world human activist mission and just adds &quot;What if some of them are Garou?&quot;. And the thinking stops right then and there. That is such a lame premise! The way it's written the fact they're Garou adds nothing to this. Okay, the Garou have supernatural powers... So what? It still all amounts to them just doing the same things these human activists already do. The WtA-premise is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541286#post1541286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if one of the frequent complaints against W5 werewolves is that they are not heroes enough, getting involved against human trafficking only if there is some hint at a Pentex front ... well, they would be quite touchy heroes, to put it mildly, when confronted by one of the biggest tragedies of these recent times.</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>All previous W5 work includes Fomori as bad guys when it isn't the Cult of Fenris/BSD or Garou who have fallen to Hauglosk. I'm just following the guidelines set down by W5.</li> <li>Going after whatever human evil even if there's no confirmed presence of Bane Spirits or Fomori... That's called the Cult of Fenris agenda in W5. The Cult of Fenris gets chastised by W5 for &quot;seeing the Wyrm in everything&quot;. W5 precisely doesn't want you to do what you're describing.</li> <li>Because there's a reason you put Fomori in there, why you have Pentex and it's about the war against the Wyrm. You put some distance between that and the real world. What you're proposing instead is to ignore the animism, the Wyrm and all that. Instead, you want to put a real-world-issue in front of the players, make the opposition mundane humans with no connection to the supernatural and then have werewolf-PCs use their violent powers against them. Additionally, at that point, this would just be a game about terrorism (using violent means to produce political change) involving real-world-issues. You would need an even longer &quot;Considerate Play&quot;-section than the one in the W5 corebook if you want the game to be about that.</li> <li>And again, this also amounts to just throwing the WtA-setting into the trash-bin. Because in this conception spirits, Garou, the Wyrm... none of that matters. You're just doing a game about a real-world-issue and for some reason the PCs are werewolves. You don't need any WtA-concepts for this.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T09:48:45-07:00","id":1541293,"title":"","content":"But the Sept's writeup explicitly mentions Cult of Fenris bad guys: &quot;. <i>It had lost a ship to the Libyan coast guard and an entire Garou pack to an assault by the Cult of Fenris. They believed that the Sept of the Water\u2019s Birth had to be stopped because they were allowing potentially Wyrm-tainted people into Cult territory</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, the Sept doesn't indulge in terrorism at all, it's plainly based on the activities of real-world NGOs with a supernatural twist. It's hardly the first instance of a supernatural redressing of something real in the history of WOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T10:07:26-07:00","id":1541295,"title":"","content":"One issue with the Water Birth sept's concept, is that the rescue is the EASY part. That is the part that I feel takes it from a good idea to one I'd rather not touch; There is a massive issue regarding WHERE these rescued immigrants go to. Which might end up resulting in a lot of IRL arguments at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T10:11:41-07:00","id":1541296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541266#post1541266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a w5 enjoyer. I'm enjoying my long campaign.<br /> I like this game as a third game about werewolves.<br /> <br /> This is my opinion: this book is utter garbage.<br /> It actually betrays even the premises of w5 core book. The npc are a bunch of complainers and they are presented as more human than human. Exactly the opposite of the game premise of &quot;wrong answers for the right problem&quot; or &quot;behead those motherfuckers who are exploiting the earth&quot;. Vaguely very human characters with no true solutions or just inspired by real life people. This books looks like a bad way to go back to some legacy content, and it does it in the worst way possible. Albrecht is a joke. Elders did that, Elders ruined this, Elders wronged those. The werewolf society is very authoritarian. Now suddenly, Elders are afraid to give orders or to do something &quot;&quot;because of fear to lose power or retaliation&quot;&quot;. The new hope are the young ones: all the solutions proposed in this book are extremely fucking human. Rage is not even mentioned. The tragedy of being a rampaging monster is absent. They even massacrated our buddies, Konietzsko and Tvarivich. They want the Cult of fenris as the big bad but what they describe looks like standard get of fenris from 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> I may say that I like great hunts, a bunch of mechanics, and even the rough way the garou talk between them, but at its core to me it looks like an extremely bad way to trying to appeal older players.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm not a fan of W5, I have to agree.<br /> <br /> Backpedaling your premises to cater to old fans isn't the most considerate move once you already built a new base. Making your new game better on its own terms is a much better approach.<br /> <br /> Even because, how much does W5 still have to change to actually bring the old players back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T10:12:21-07:00","id":1541297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541293#post1541293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Sept's writeup explicitly mentions Cult of Fenris bad guys: &quot;. <i>It had lost a ship to the Libyan coast guard and an entire Garou pack to an assault by the Cult of Fenris. They believed that the Sept of the Water\u2019s Birth had to be stopped because they were allowing potentially Wyrm-tainted people into Cult territory</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's get the whole quote because we're talking about some tone-deaf, poorly thought-out writing here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the years since the sept was established, all of its members have been arrested at least once. It had lost a ship to the Libyan coast guard and an entire Garou pack to an assault by the Cult of Fenris. They believed that the Sept of the Water\u2019s Birth had to be stopped because they were allowing potentially Wyrm-tainted people into Cult territory. The fact that the people saved by the Sept are not more Wyrm-afflicted than any other random selection of people doesn\u2019t seem to matter to the Cult. </div> </div> </div>What this section is referencing is the fear of anti-immigration-activists of good refugees and bad refugess (who are criminals and so on). And so you can't just be tolerant of people moving in and should be paranoid and fearful instead. It's a tone-deaf, badly written section because right there at the end, the text says the anti-immigration-sentiment is right and yes there ARE good and bad refugees but you should be tolerant nonetheless. And for that, the writer makes the truly bad choice to use &quot;Wyrm-afflicted&quot; as an WtA-analogue. Why is it bad, you may wonder? Have you ever heard in the history of WtA of a Garou who argued that among this certain number of people this certain amount of &quot;Wyrm-taint&quot; is normal and therefore everything's okay? Of course not! If there is a Fomori, you don't hear a Garou say &quot;Well, among this neighborhood of 2000 people, one Fomori is normal. No need to fret.&quot;.<br /> <br /> So on one hand you have the Cult of Fenris go after Wyrm-afflicted humans which is something every Garou does. And on the other hand, the notion that the Cult of Fenris cares about immigration-policy and is invested in stopping illegal immigration is the same kind of silliness as just making a Sept all about human activism. This has nothing to do with them being Garou at that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541293#post1541293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the Sept doesn't indulge in terrorism at all, it's plainly based on the activities of real-world NGOs with a supernatural twist. It's hardly the first instance of a supernatural redressing of something real in the history of WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there is NO supernatural twist. The Garou are entirely incidental.<br /> <br /> And I'm talking about W5 specifically, not the entirety of WOD. Besides, you still haven't addressed how you square that with how W5 talks about the Cult of Fenris.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T11:10:43-07:00","id":1541301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541297#post1541297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's get the whole quote because we're talking about some tone-deaf, poorly thought-out writing here:<br /> <br /> <br /> What this section is referencing is the fear of anti-immigration-activists of good refugees and bad refugess (who are criminals and so on). And so you can't just be tolerant of people moving in and should be paranoid and fearful instead. It's a tone-deaf, badly written section because right there at the end, the text says the anti-immigration-sentiment is right and yes there ARE good and bad refugees but you should be tolerant nonetheless. And for that, the writer makes the truly bad choice to use &quot;Wyrm-afflicted&quot; as an WtA-analogue. Why is it bad, you may wonder? Have you ever heard in the history of WtA of a Garou who argued that among this certain number of people this certain amount of &quot;Wyrm-taint&quot; is normal and therefore everything's okay? Of course not! If there is a Fomori, you don't hear a Garou say &quot;Well, among this neighborhood of 2000 people, one Fomori is normal. No need to fret.&quot;.<br /> <br /> So on one hand you have the Cult of Fenris go after Wyrm-afflicted humans which is something every Garou does. And on the other hand, the notion that the Cult of Fenris cares about immigration-policy and is invested in stopping illegal immigration is the same kind of silliness as just making a Sept all about human activism. This has nothing to do with them being Garou at that point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except there is NO supernatural twist. The Garou are entirely incidental.<br /> <br /> And I'm talking about W5 specifically, not the entirety of WOD. Besides, you still haven't addressed how you square that with how W5 talks about the Cult of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>And of course all the npc from the Italian sept are not italians, because we italians are known R A C I S T S and Fenris worshipping","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T13:27:34-07:00","id":1541303,"title":"","content":"I'm still over here pondering why there aren't a lot more bodies if every member of the Sept has been arrested at some point......cos putting Garou in handcuffs is invariably a recipe for badness.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T16:37:28-07:00","id":1541307,"title":"","content":"I do also like the idea of the Legendary Rites and while I agree it has heavy LARP vibes that could definitely be something worth fleshing out and making use of. Ritual reenactment has a long and venerable tradition and the idea that the ritual\u2019s narrative can go different ways depending on how it\u2019s carried out with different spiritual ramifications has some real juice to if imo - it reminds me somewhat of how something like Tarot has standard images and references but the peculiarities of their particular arrangement and how the reader responds to it can make every reading different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T17:35:06-07:00","id":1541310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541296#post1541296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'm not a fan of W5, I have to agree.<br /> <br /> Backpedaling your premises to cater to old fans isn't the most considerate move once you already built a new base. Making your new game better on its own terms is a much better approach.<br /> <br /> Even because, how much does W5 still have to change to actually bring the old players back?</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, trying to appeal to older players in the way they're doing here is even worse than if they hadn't even bothered, because there's still that air of &quot;the legacy lore, characters, and goals are bad and cringe and only these New Garou will save us&quot; all over the writing. Which is made even worse because these new Garou still barely even do anything. They still haven't fixed the issue of being dismissive of real action beyond beating up mooks and sulking in your own sept until the world keels over (Not to mention doubling down on being dismissive of animism and oral histories. You don't remember things from 20-30 years ago? Really? <i>Reeeeally?)</i><br /> <br /> W5 really needs to find one thing and commit to it if it's going to survive as its own game. Is it about redemption from the mistakes of your ancestors? Trying to save what's left in the world that can be saved? Is it about every wolf for themselves in the face of the Apocalypse? Pick one and stick to it, because as it is, all of these messages are contradicting each other and making a huge mess of awkward doomerism. This book really didn't help by dragging in a bunch of legacy content and executing it badly, and imo it'd be better off if it just stopped trying and just became more of its own thing apart from old editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T19:24:47-07:00","id":1541316,"title":"","content":"Agreed....if &quot; We're bringing back Legacy NPCs but they are all invariably utterly shite&quot; is a plan to appeal to Legacy folks its not a good one......and kinda reflects the general attitude to Legacy Players and STs from a certain subsect of W5 fans and officials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 08-31-2024, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T19:38:10-07:00","id":1541318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541233#post1541233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I liked the Stargazer section more than the corebook-one but that section once again focuses more on the &quot;fight smarter, not harder&quot;-aspect which is something all Garou in W5 should aspire to. Rather, what W5 should do since they want them to be these mysterious non-playable &quot;allies&quot; is to emphasize their enigmatic behavior, I think. Like, a Stargazer comes around and tells you the way to get a Pentex-Front to go bankrupt is to do ridiculous stuff like eating noodles at a bus-stop every day at a certain time and buying specific flowers from a shop. Stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funnily enough that's actually one of the reason that the Eastern Concordat is founded. The tribes that make up that alliance, which includes the Stargazers (kinda they were absorbed into the Children of Gaia) knows that the current way of doing things is going nowhere and they want to change it. This is also part of the reason the Garou nation splits (another is disagreements on how the garou treats Kinfolk).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also here what the WtE author might do to integrate W5 into WtE lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can definitely see that. Even the 'twisted upbringing flaw' reflects exactly that: a Garou who was only offered a highly distorted view of the Garou and needs to undergo extensive deprogramming.<br /> <br /> Playing with the 'unreality' idea of the W5 universe crossing over to WtE, there's a Pentex version of Werewolf: the Apocalypse they put out that almost hilariously features a lot of aspects of the w5 verse. Imagine a game setting where Pentex did, in fact, release their version of Werewolf (Lycanthrope: the Rapture). Canonically it was never released, but maybe in an alt universe iIt became a household name like D&amp;D. Suddenly, you have a fuckton of Lost Cubs who believe that game world is real and begin reaching out to work with the makers (the 'fuck everyone' elders of w5) who are looking to trap the players in increasingly amoral missions until it becomes imperative for the player characters to go 'no fucking way' and start looking around themselves with the intention to see through the ruse (and you'd have to work with the players that they expect the subversion.)<br /> </div> </div> </div>I personally would have gone with a more Matrix inspired plot and even have an heavily extended version subplot from the latest movie where the Big Bad gaslights Neo into thinking he's just a video game dev past his prime. Just put Albrecht in the part of Neo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-31-2024, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T05:36:14-07:00","id":1541329,"title":"","content":"The Fenrir writing seems rather odd since they're not really acting like werewolf extremists and more a group that is proactively antagonistic to other werewolves ala classic black spiral and particularly odd considering the Black spirals shades of grey (A tribe explicitly stating to be enthusiastic rapists and groomers). I suspect the change from werewolf nazi's to werewolf extremists came really late in development and a lot of stuff had already been written or they're trying to just really push the idea of the Fenrir as the antagonist werewolves.<br /> <br /> I'm also somewhat bemused by what they're doing with Jonas Albrecht considering he's just his dad from previous editions now. Which seems weirdly pointless unless you're trying to be insult legacy fans.<br /> <br /> As a bi person ross the she wolf feels a little...awkward in a way I can't quite pin down. similar to Rudy from anarchs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T05:47:18-07:00","id":1541330,"title":"","content":"So if anyone want's tom compare all of Sharttred Nation to just one chapter of WtE. You can talk about the it in the thread here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview\"> WtE Final layout Preview - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Well as it says on the tin this is the Preview for the final layout of Book 1 of the (Hopefully) five book run of Werewolf the Essentials. Source: https://www.tumblr.com/werewolfessentials/758186097516871680/for-todays-werewolf-wednesday-rather-than?source=share There's not much else to say that I haven't said before </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T07:01:11-07:00","id":1541332,"title":"","content":"I think this is the most insulting section of the whole moot chapter. It is one thing to have a quick roll if the galliard player is tired. But they don't even imply that players COULD tell stories at the moot. Just the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Besides, if the moot is just rolls, a big part of the point of them to the game is lost.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:unset\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T12:03:43-07:00","id":1541345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541332#post1541332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is the most insulting section of the whole moot chapter. It is one thing to have a quick roll if the galliard player is tired. But they don't even imply that players COULD tell stories at the moot. Just the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Besides, if the moot is just rolls, a big part of the point of them to the game is lost.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:unset\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It is insulting but it will never beat this.<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"512\" height=\"513\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/6Q9xPtL8/image.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/6Q9xPtL8/image.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/6Q9xPtL8/image.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> Even if we ignore that it implies all Garou are sticking to the oral storytelling (nevermind we had glyphs in the past editions) and that oral storytelling is shit, it also implies no Garou from 80s and 90 ever took notes in more modern ways Even Glass Walkers. Are they stupid? Do they expect me to believe this.<br /> Oh and most Garou are what, in their 20s? Who taught them? Did all of their teachers die? How are there are tribes and Garou Nation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T12:44:56-07:00","id":1541349,"title":"","content":"To add to that, remember this bit from the Introduction that we actually saw in the preview: &quot;Modern communications technology means that Garou can talk to each other easier than ever before, and so have realized that their immutable traditions and culture are often actually entirely local. Other Garou in other places do things differently.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's nothing in this book that supports this. W5 still doesn't have a global perspective. The Amazon War gets mentioned in this book as one of those legacy-things they brought back. But was there any part in this book where any space was dedicated to presenting an actual W5 version (like a Sept or a sample-character) of what Garou-life is like in the Amazon Rainforest...? Of course not. The book dropped that little cheeky reference - and that was it.<br /> <br /> Hell, the glyphs you mentioned, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27335\" data-vbnamecard=\"27335\">Technoma</a> , there's a sidebar on pg 43 that rehashes the old idea of Glyphs including &quot;When Garou use them, they are traditionally carved with claws or klaives.\u200b&quot;. Even though part of the redesign of W5 was to take all the Glyphs and make them look more cluttered (and often in a way where it's hard to imagine a Garou used their claws to create these). And the idea that despite all these shortcomings when it comes to lorekeeping and historical memory, the idea of Garou still calling themselves Garou and also still having this common language with these Glyphs is just bizarre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T13:52:35-07:00","id":1541357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541349#post1541349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, the glyphs you mentioned, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27335\" data-vbnamecard=\"27335\">Technoma</a> , there's a sidebar on pg 43 that rehashes the old idea of Glyphs including &quot;When Garou use them, they are traditionally carved with claws or klaives.&quot;. Even though part of the redesign of W5 was to take all the Glyphs and make them look more cluttered (and often in a way where it's hard to imagine a Garou used their claws to create these). And the idea that despite all these shortcomings when it comes to lorekeeping and historical memory, the idea of Garou still calling themselves Garou and also still having this common language with these Glyphs is just bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much of the lore seems to solely exist to make the garou look bad, or utterly incompetent. In ways that make no sense if you give it a bit more thought. There are actual systems in WoD to create a sort of knowledge loss, the fog of ages in VtR and what the mummies in Curse deal with. More importantly, spots are left blank so the STs can insert their own plot elements into them.<br /> <br /> W5 has no forgetting mechanic, it has no stated reason why the garou can't know of the past. Instead they, in an edition supposed to be more considerate than Legacy, outright state that oral histories and such are flawed and result in information lost. If they aren't just saying garou are too stupid to know their own history. There is no &quot;ST can insert history here&quot; mentality, instead the books say garou are just incompetent.<br /> <br /> Or that you can play a Moon Cult member as per book, but you CAN'T play a Stargazer even though Gazers still share basic nation beliefs while the Moon Cults don't.<br /> <br /> Or that the faction that is supposed to be on the same side as the PCs, Cult of Fenris, is presented more dangerous than the actual wyrmtainted werewolves. Robbing any sort of nuance from the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T14:05:19-07:00","id":1541358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541345#post1541345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is insulting but it will never beat this.<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"512\" height=\"513\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/6Q9xPtL8/image.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/6Q9xPtL8/image.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/6Q9xPtL8/image.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> Even if we ignore that it implies all Garou are sticking to the oral storytelling (nevermind we had glyphs in the past editions) and that oral storytelling is shit, it also implies no Garou from 80s and 90 ever took notes in more modern ways Even Glass Walkers. Are they stupid? Do they expect me to believe this.<br /> Oh and most Garou are what, in their 20s? Who taught them? Did all of their teachers die? How are there are tribes and Garou Nation?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that view of history is kinda simullar to some authoritarian regimes like the nazis and the Russian Federation. And they're not the most stable countries...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T14:15:36-07:00","id":1541359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541357#post1541357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much of the lore seems to solely exist to make the garou look bad, or utterly incompetent. In ways that make no sense if you give it a bit more thought. There are actual systems in WoD to create a sort of knowledge loss, the fog of ages in VtR and what the mummies in Curse deal with. More importantly, spots are left blank so the STs can insert their own plot elements into them.<br /> <br /> W5 has no forgetting mechanic, it has no stated reason why the garou can't know of the past. Instead they, in an edition supposed to be more considerate than Legacy, outright state that oral histories and such are flawed and result in information lost. If they aren't just saying garou are too stupid to know their own history. There is no &quot;ST can insert history here&quot; mentality, instead the books say garou are just incompetent.<br /> <br /> Or that you can play a Moon Cult member as per book, but you CAN'T play a Stargazer even though Gazers still share basic nation beliefs while the Moon Cults don't.<br /> <br /> Or that the faction that is supposed to be on the same side as the PCs, Cult of Fenris, is presented more dangerous than the actual wyrmtainted werewolves. Robbing any sort of nuance from the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I don't like it but it is what it is. And yet, even on their terms, this stuff doesn't work. Moon Cults are underwritten. The one thing that could stand out here and they barely put any effort in to fully flesh it out. Gaian Cults is the same deal! What a waste...<br /> <br /> The way they're going it wouldn't surprise me if their big idea for the next W5 supplement is to resurrect Samuel Haight... And the explanation for why and how this happens will be even more bizarre than anyone can imagine right now. &quot;Gaia's Howl triggered a time-portal and a still alive Samuel Haight from 1999 stumbled through it only to find himself in 2025.&quot; It will be shit like that, I bet... Just barely thought-through trite stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T14:34:03-07:00","id":1541360,"title":"","content":"Something which occurs is aside from stetching narrative suspention of disbelief and being quite disrespectful of oral history, im not entirely clear why this discision was made for the writting. How does the game benifit from this? How is it improved? What purpose does it achieve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-01-2024, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T16:29:48-07:00","id":1541365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541332#post1541332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is the most insulting section of the whole moot chapter. It is one thing to have a quick roll if the galliard player is tired. But they don't even imply that players COULD tell stories at the moot. Just the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Besides, if the moot is just rolls, a big part of the point of them to the game is lost.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:unset\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/j9CUceo.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Also insulting is that, yet again, most of these are just more Garou infighting/&quot;lol aren't the Garou just so incompetent and their culture so stupid?&quot; Some of these combinations don't even make sense (Why are Stargazers and &quot;Garou tradition&quot; even here and put on the level of Fomori or banes?????)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T17:28:07-07:00","id":1541368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541360#post1541360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which occurs is aside from stetching narrative suspention of disbelief and being quite disrespectful of oral history, im not entirely clear why this discision was made for the writting. How does the game benifit from this? How is it improved? What purpose does it achieve?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking that the person who would get the most out of this is somebody who started with the W5 corebook and still knows next to nothing about WtA. But even there, I gotta wonder: When they get to that Legandary Rites section, I have a hard time believing that they'll be able to make heads or tails out of all that stuff. You <i>have to</i> look up the legacy-material to get anywhere with that. Because those bits (except for the Legendary Rite involving Ross the She-Wolf which is more on the generic side of things) are knee-deep in the muck of the meta-plot that supposedly isn't part of W5 anymore since it's a &quot;re-imagination, not a continuation&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T00:21:20-07:00","id":1541382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541360#post1541360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which occurs is aside from stetching narrative suspention of disbelief and being quite disrespectful of oral history, im not entirely clear why this discision was made for the writting. How does the game benifit from this? How is it improved? What purpose does it achieve?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I have seen in terms of reactions; People who saw Legacy as racist, fascist, utterly awful and want their game to put down any Legacy concept as flawed. I have ran into people who think this or have them come to my posts saying this.<br /> <br /> I feel it is those people that get the most out of the constant putting down of garou and the garou nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T00:48:29-07:00","id":1541383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541382#post1541382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I have seen in terms of reactions; People who saw Legacy as racist, fascist, utterly awful and want their game to put down any Legacy concept as flawed. I have ran into people who think this or have them come to my posts saying this.<br /> <br /> I feel it is those people that get the most out of the constant putting down of garou and the garou nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And no doubt they would turn around and decry Paradox for being greedy short-sighted a holes if this game line is cancelled due to they recent financial problems.<br /> <br /> Any way here's something less depressing. Here's mundus's write up for the Get.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/3RMPCh2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3RMPCh2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3RMPCh2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/stKbAmj.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/stKbAmj.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/stKbAmj.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/iGKmomt.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/iGKmomt.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/iGKmomt.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/i4XViEs.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/i4XViEs.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/i4XViEs.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/759829796004986880/hi-i-saw-your-reblogged-ask-about-wte?source=share\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/1d3ea2a500975750c48491f648f9ee0e/4c43fd936d266b72-76/s500x750/b10ae1fb574b9230ac317a90de90fbe90422030c.pnj\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/759829796004986880/hi-i-saw-your-reblogged-ask-about-wte?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> Post by @songoftrillium &middot; 1 image </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/759829796004986880/hi-i-saw-your-reblogged-ask-about-wte?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/759829796004986880/hi-i-saw-your-reblogged-ask-about-wte?source=share </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \ud83d\udcac 0&nbsp;&nbsp;\ud83d\udd01 26&nbsp;&nbsp;\u2764\ufe0f 41&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Get of Fenris (see below the cut)&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Hi!! I saw your reblogged ask about WtE redesigning the Get, and I'm curious what you can share? I'm working on my own rewrite project (it's&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> It's kinda of cross post for this thread:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview#post1540413\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview#post1540413\"> WtE Final layout Preview - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview#post1540413\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview#post1540413 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Well as it says on the tin this is the Preview for the final layout of Book 1 of the (Hopefully) five book run of Werewolf the Essentials. Source: https://www.tumblr.com/werewolfessentials/758186097516871680/for-todays-werewolf-wednesday-rather-than?source=share There's not much else to say that I haven't said before </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which also includes a Update for WtE. Unfortunately the post was Unapproved. Possibly because I posted too much pictures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T02:31:48-07:00","id":1541386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541382#post1541382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I have seen in terms of reactions; People who saw Legacy as racist, fascist, utterly awful and want their game to put down any Legacy concept as flawed. I have ran into people who think this or have them come to my posts saying this.<br /> <br /> I feel it is those people that get the most out of the constant putting down of garou and the garou nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense (even if I disagree) why they wouldn't use the old lore but it doesn't explain the new lore or more accurately lack of it, when I though the Anarchs and Verbenna were badly written in setting I did a re-write. I didn't just shrug whenever anyone needed to interact with them in any context.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine anyone finds this non-commital satisfying as lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T06:33:54-07:00","id":1541390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541386#post1541386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes sense (even if I disagree) why they wouldn't use the old lore but it doesn't explain the new lore or more accurately lack of it, when I though the Anarchs and Verbenna were badly written in setting I did a re-write. I didn't just shrug whenever anyone needed to interact with them in any context.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine anyone finds this non-commital satisfying as lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't seem to see the lack of new lore, because what matters is that the old lore is insulted and constantly put down as flawed. It is mostly just getting purity points, as the saying goes, what looks good is better than what IS good.<br /> <br /> Because none of this truly affects how the actual game is played. Even if the lore is lacking, the core W5 game is still about a pack, a caern and so on. Fighting the Wyrm because otherwise they'd have nothing to do. Only now they are pushed to do even less than before.<br /> <br /> As you said, there is very little new lore. Because vast majority of the core and Shattered Nation are more focused on what NOT to do than what to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T10:08:06-07:00","id":1541399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541329#post1541329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a bi person ross the she wolf feels a little...awkward in a way I can't quite pin down. similar to Rudy from anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to get back to this because I had the same reaction. Something feels off about that Loresheet. I think it's just this broad gesturing at various stuff, LGBTQ+, minorities, pollution... but it never coheres. Like, he's described as a <i>proud </i>gay man but then one of the dots is &quot;Transwolf&quot; which allows you to change your sex while shapeshifting. And how the minority-part only gets emphasized on the fifth dot. Also, how it just starts: &quot;Fifth dot - Pride: You are a member of a minority group.&quot; Like it's an organization or something. It just feels off.<br /> <br /> It's similar to that one section where this one Pack is summoning this Ancestor-Spirit called Old Trucker. I get what they're trying to say but the way it's written... Really odd style and characterization and it all felt a bit off-putting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T10:44:00-07:00","id":1541400,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;A history of the Garou is both impossible and reductive. The stories of the past that werewolves tell are oral histories, part legend and part reality, revised, reinterpreted, and redone, according to the needs of the generation doing the telling. They contain multiple narratives that are all considered to be true. The finer details, locations, and players in these grand dramas may shift with the times, and with the storytellers spinning the tale for those listening to them. </i>&quot; <b>- W5 core, p.22</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia? Because the historical events involved in it date to various times across myriad locations, to say with any certainty is impossible, and even spirits speak of it in terms unsuited to the physical world. </i>&quot; <b>-W5 core, p.37</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Much of the Garou\u2019s history is oral, more within the realm of legend and even self-mythology than a true history. Given the animistic perspective of Garou, when one says, \u201cthe mighty Silver Fang rode upon Falcon\u2019s back,\u201d that might literally mean a werewolf rode an enormous falcon in a legendary time, or it may mean that a falcon-spirit carried the werewolf, or even that Falcon himself transported the werewolf through the Umbra.</i><br /> <br /> <i>So it goes with the Litany, a code of Garou custom that\u2019s equally as impressionistic and open to interpretation as the animistic lens through which werewolves see the world.&quot;</i> <b>-W5 core,p.46</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Litany is an imperfect set of rules by which to wage a guerilla war of resistance during an ongoing Apocalypse. Those rules mean different things at different times to different werewolves, and the oral tradition of the Garou is rife with the Litany being used to justify self-dealing or even atrocity. </i>&quot; <b>-W5 core, p.47</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Above and beyond the tribes and the septs, there used to be something called the Garou Nation. It was understood that all Garou were united in their war against the forces of the Wyrm.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Some dispute whether this was ever really true. Were the Garou of old really united in a global nation in the mythical prehistory of Garou legend at a time when humans had barely managed to get from one continent to another&quot;</i> <b>-Shattered Nation, p.37</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Garou are creatures of the present, their traditions built on oral storytelling. This means that factual accuracy is often not considered particularly important as long as the broad outlines fit what the crowd at the moot wants to hear. The stories of Garou from the '80s and '90s are already ancient history, having happened before most Garou today were even born.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Garou legends are notoriously difficult to date accurately. When was the War of Rage or the Impergium? In the Middle Ages? In the Stone Age? Who knows, and the spirits are no help either. Their sense of time is so different that it\u2019s impossible to translate into human reckoning.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>-Shattered Nation, p.40</b><br /> <br /> These are all the times I could find in which W5 outright said oral history is bad.<br /> <br /> Especially on the Litany part, not only is there an auspice for it, but also the whole point of it is that it is a song that is simplified into the tenets we know. Many things are put into songs so you remember them.<br /> <br /> Also, if they wanted the history to stay secret, there are actual mechanics and valid lore reasons to use. Instead it all is laid at the feet of incompetence and oral history being faulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T15:29:15-07:00","id":1541412,"title":"","content":"The thought occurs that W5 is like a lot of the problems that the CoG faced, writ large. For the longest time, the CoGs basically had no culture other than 60s counterculture beats from the US, and thus, little, if any, substance to them, with a muted stake in the struggles of W:tA. This book seems to just compound on that problem, because it continues to try and fly with no guidance from grounding, no flight plan, and no prospect of finding a runway to touch down when it needs refueling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T01:44:29-07:00","id":1541435,"title":"","content":"What I also don't get is the implications.<br /> Do Garou not write at all? Even though without kinfolk most Garou were born in a normal family. Did no one write in numerous human languages those garou would learn as their mother tongue?<br /> <br /> Do Garou abandon writing the moment they change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T02:17:09-07:00","id":1541436,"title":"","content":"The forgetting is only the first part that is so baffling. Because the follow-up is also the implication that after the knowledge of the history has been forgotten throughout generations, the response to that was these newer Garou supposedly thinking &quot;What happened back then...? I dunno.&quot;. And then they just moved on! Even some of the most ancient human cultures already cared about memorializing their past in some fashion (like having a tradition of oral storytelling). Even if it isn't 100% the truth, you'd think they would come up with some sort of story they could look at as a documentation of their shared history. But what W5 is suggesting is that after the amnesia, there was simply no attempt to create any sort of history for themselves. &quot;The Garou Nation? Dunno what that was... was it a decade? A century? A millenia? Who knows.&quot;. That sort of ambivalence would only make sense if these newer Garou stopped caring altogether about being a Garou and didn't identify like that anymore.<br /> <br /> And you see that in the Legendary Rites. They are all these recent events (although of course according to Shattered Nation, the 80s and 90s are already &quot;ancient history&quot;). There's no creation-myth of Garou interacting with Gaia and Luna for the first time, no Rite about the Impergium and the Concord or any myths about how these Tribes with their respective Patron Spirits came to be... It's all just shrugged off in favor of more recent stuff. You'd think the most prevalent Legendary Rites would be these events that are fundamental to the Garou's sense of history and identity rather than having a Rite about one Garou's adventures from a couple of years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T03:14:22-07:00","id":1541437,"title":"","content":"Humans have oral history that can lead someone to a rock face to collect ochre 45,000 years after it was first discovered.......Garou have oral history that can't recall where someone rediscovered a sacred site nine months ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T03:20:45-07:00","id":1541438,"title":"","content":"Something Ana, I think, said about W5 Garou religious concepts tending towards using Christian nomenclature and structure rather than animist is really quite prevalent as I read through SN again even moreso than it was in the Core. I'm not sure if that's due to the writers backgrounds or if that was an editorial/Developer decision...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T06:01:18-07:00","id":1541441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541438#post1541438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something Ana, I think, said about W5 Garou religious concepts tending towards using Christian nomenclature and structure rather than animist is really quite prevalent as I read through SN again even moreso than it was in the Core. I'm not sure if that's due to the writers backgrounds or if that was an editorial/Developer decision...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, even regarding things not directly related to Christianity but are part of the culture it has created in Europe.<br /> <br /> There is this air of 'we have passed the age of ignorance' to the text, where everything should be questioned and nothing is sacred. Like some katana wielding atheists few years back, W5 treats sacredness as willful blindness and ignorance. Which also means that everything is now fair game as long as it is not outwardly racist.<br /> <br /> But that is now universal, that is very much a product of people leaving the Christian church. The people W5 says it is considerate of aren't that irrelevant and don't treat sacredness as a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T06:41:56-07:00","id":1541444,"title":"","content":"There's this exchange that one young Pack has with this Ancestor Spirit called Old Trucker (who's a Native American Garou who lived in the 50s):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Old Trucker: Not a false descriptor. These primal words were kept incomplete among the walking wolves of all lands, but in particular right here in our nation. By the spirits and men of this land. This Kanien\u2019kehaka nation. Anyway, in this corner of Turtle Island, as you say, the GEHRAU (whispered growl tone) living among the people of OH (Flint) kept the primal tongue for centuries while your overseas ancestors lost pretty central parts of it, as you lost your souls. The howls of the hunt were gone,<br /> replaced by words scavenged from the humans. Here, they were conserved in oral tradition. We abided by the Impergium on this side of the ocean, and so we<br /> honored the wolf, rather than slaughtering it, like medieval man was wont to do, in search of arable land.<br /> <br /> Fast-Paw: So, then us Europeans came and we learned the words back!<br /> <br /> Abbie: No. Remember Colonialism 101? We killed them all before they taught us. First Nation\u2019s elders call us Wyrm-comers for a reason. So yes, the spirits know more words than us. Now shut up, stupid ahroun!\u200b </div> </div> </div>This section doesn't really distinguish between talking about human history and Garou history. Also, this makes it quite confusing what the Garou do and don't know about their past. Also for this edition that supposedly wanted things to be more universal and go away from tying Garou to human ethnicity and regions, this section is pretty much in favor of making distinctions along those lines. In this section, it really starts to matter again what these characters' heritage and ancestry are.<br /> <br /> And it does come off like Old Trucker's implying here that the Impergium was a good thing and other Garou like those in Europe were fools for abandoning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T07:23:29-07:00","id":1541445,"title":"","content":"Is it me or is Abbie basically saying they shouldn't learn the old words due to the history?<br /> <br /> Also, this implies that the garou of Turtle Island DID record things... but European garou came and now no one records anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T08:12:37-07:00","id":1541452,"title":"","content":"This is how it ends:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abbie: Good job, you fucking stinkdogs. Now, keep your piss in your bladder, strip off everything you don\u2019t want blood on, shoot up, do your vocal warmups, and grab something sharp. We\u2019re going old-school tonight.<br /> <br /> And \u2013 in case I was unclear during the Rite \u2013 as far as I know, none of us have even a speck of Potawatomi in us. Prepare some scars or atonement and be ready to exercise that colonialist guilt by the pint. Bring klaives. </div> </div> </div>I think the idea here is that European colonialism is directly tied to European Garou. It comes off like the writing's making Europe the center of the universe. The only place where modernization, imperialism and industrialization happened (which strengthened the Wyrm) was Europe. And the rest of the world was this paradisical setting that was ravaged by European colonialism. And somehow European Garou are a part of this - who then also ruined things for the other Garou in the world.<br /> <br /> But it also illustrates this &quot;White guilt&quot;-perspective where the European/Western perspective is still in the driver-seat. None of the people in this Pack are Native American, so their ancestors were the protagonists. As colonialists they did bad things but they were the ones in control, the main-characters of that time. But now these kids like Abbie know what happened back then was bad. And it's still their story because now it's about them making amends for what happened in the past. You have that Native American there as a mentor-figure who chides them by reminding them of their ancestor's misdeeds but then he's also there to applaud them for trying to do better. But at no point are there Native Americans in the driver-seat here. Back then they were victims and now this Native American Spirit is just there to make these white kids feel good about themselves for trying to do better from then on.<br /> <br /> Again, just spitballing here but wouldn't it have made more sense with all the dynamics I mentioned in the last post and this one if the Ritemaster/Theurge had been a Native American Garou who summoned this Ancestor Spirit? Why did they make it about a Pack of young, white Garou and a Native American Ancestor-Spirit...?<br /> <br /> Later on, Abbie gets killed by a vampire and there's this email on pg 85 where one of her Packmates references her attitude was &quot;new nation steps back and thinks&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T08:45:51-07:00","id":1541453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541452#post1541452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how it ends:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the idea here is that European colonialism is directly tied to European Garou. It comes off like the writing's making Europe the center of the universe. The only place where modernization, imperialism and industrialization happened (which strengthened the Wyrm) was Europe. And the rest of the world was this paradisical setting that was ravaged by European colonialism. And somehow European Garou are a part of this - who then also ruined things for the other Garou in the world.<br /> <br /> But it also illustrates this &quot;White guilt&quot;-perspective where the European/Western perspective is still in the driver-seat. None of the people in this Pack are Native American, so their ancestors were the protagonists. As colonialists they did bad things but they were the ones in control, the main-characters of that time. But now these kids like Abbie know what happened back then was bad. And it's still their story because now it's about them making amends for what happened in the past. You have that Native American there as a mentor-figure who chides them by reminding them of their ancestor's misdeeds but then he's also there to applaud them for trying to do better. But at no point are there Native Americans in the driver-seat here. Back then they were victims and now this Native American Spirit is just there to make these white kids feel good about themselves for trying to do better from then on.<br /> <br /> Again, just spitballing here but wouldn't it have made more sense with all the dynamics I mentioned in the last post and this one if the Ritemaster/Theurge had been a Native American Garou who summoned this Ancestor Spirit? Why did they make it about a Pack of young, white Garou and a Native American Ancestor-Spirit...?<br /> <br /> Later on, Abbie gets killed by a vampire and there's this email on pg 85 where one of her Packmates references her attitude was &quot;new nation steps back and thinks&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very simplified, I feel because none of the writers felt comfortable writing a native american character. There is also this mentality, most likely accidental, that implies that ALL native american garou were killed off and now exist only as spirits.<br /> <br /> The way Abbie handles things is also weird, she is treating this whole thing as an apology to the ancestor spirit and focuses on self-mutilating suffering. But she also is refusing any sort of learning from the ancestor spirit for her pack. As you said, not creating distinction between the humans and garou at all.<br /> <br /> Also, if this rite is supposed to call upon an ancestor spirit, why is the focus on hurting oneself. Shouldn't a rite like that rely more on using things that were dear to the ancestor? I could see a contrition rite done to North Wind that involved bloodletting, but to a non-violent ancestor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T13:47:34-07:00","id":1541483,"title":"","content":"Abbie sounds a bit of a pretentious arse lol.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity did first nation tribes explicitly not hunt wolves as suggested here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T17:41:27-07:00","id":1541495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I also don't get is the implications.<br /> Do Garou not write at all? Even though without kinfolk most Garou were born in a normal family. Did no one write in numerous human languages those garou would learn as their mother tongue?<br /> <br /> Do Garou abandon writing the moment they change?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in legacy editions, the Silver Record would often be written down. The opening story of 2e (not Legacy Rite, but the text intro) involved a newly-changed cub waking up in a lodge that had the glyphs carved into every corner of its construction (and the enemy soon followed, so the Garou who had memorized it had to burn it down). The same cub is the opening narrator of The Silver Record (the W:tA book).<br /> <br /> That just continues to support my conjecture that nothing after 1993 is getting traction in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T05:04:35-07:00","id":1541523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541483#post1541483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abbie sounds a bit of a pretentious arse lol.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity did first nation tribes explicitly not hunt wolves as suggested here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the thing, they hunted them, either to manage populations, to protect their stocks of meat from packs scavenging or specifically for cultural/religious reasons, as parts of the hunted wolves were used in rites. <br /> <br /> So the whole &quot;we didn't hunted wolves&quot; is purely made up here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T09:06:05-07:00","id":1541534,"title":"","content":"There certainly wasn't a universal avoidance of killing wolves; the Navajo used wolf skins in certain ceremonies. It shouldn't be assumed in turn that all groups did at all times just because it's not true as a universal statement, though. It's not uncommon for there to be animals it's taboo to kill. What <i>is</i> true, as far as I know, is that there weren't organized campaigns of slaughter like there were in much of Europe during the period of wolf extirpation there. The usual rejoinder is to simply assert that Native American tribes couldn't have extirpated wolves as Europeans did, and assert that they would've if they could've; I think that's largely bullshit and Europe's relationship with wolves was unusually dysfunctional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T18:00:20-07:00","id":1541668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541534#post1541534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There certainly wasn't a universal avoidance of killing wolves; the Navajo used wolf skins in certain ceremonies. It shouldn't be assumed in turn that all groups did at all times just because it's not true as a universal statement, though. It's not uncommon for there to be animals it's taboo to kill. What <i>is</i> true, as far as I know, is that there weren't organized campaigns of slaughter like there were in much of Europe during the period of wolf extirpation there. The usual rejoinder is to simply assert that Native American tribes couldn't have extirpated wolves as Europeans did, and assert that they would've if they could've; I think that's largely bullshit and Europe's relationship with wolves was unusually dysfunctional.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it was a matter of difference between European and American life<br /> <br /> As opposed to the way native American lived, Europeans were extremely dependant on sheep's, goats and other herded animals. Which brought up wolves attracted to the apparent easy prey. Starting our long enmity with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T18:16:07-07:00","id":1541670,"title":"","content":"So we created dogs to guard the herds....and then neglected dogs which went feral....and killed way more sheep than the Wolves ever did....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T18:49:32-07:00","id":1541672,"title":"","content":"Cruel twists of life - anatomically modern humans were more open to living alongside wolves than the Neanderthals, having never seen wild canids like them before. Humans then drove Neanderthals extinct (not hard given their difficulties, but still), and took up the Neanderthal's antagonism of wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T21:02:41-07:00","id":1541677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541668#post1541668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, it was a matter of difference between European and American life<br /> <br /> As opposed to the way native American lived, Europeans were extremely dependant on sheep's, goats and other herded animals. Which brought up wolves attracted to the apparent easy prey. Starting our long enmity with them</div> </div> </div> </div>There've been Native Americans who herded--they got the animals after 1492, but it was important to their lifestyles. As far as I know they <i>still</i> had a less fucked up relationship with the wolf than Europeans did. But this shouldn't be too surprising. It was a common ideological belief in much of Western Europe that land not turned to human cultivation was wasted and ought to be turned to human use and that the wolf was in some way connected with evil powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T13:10:29-07:00","id":1541697,"title":"","content":"hmmm bear with me because I'm a brit so my experience is minimal but I've been told a lot of white writers put first nation groups on a pedestal as somehow more in tune with nature as opposed to the eco-social ramifications of high population density and feudal/early era economics. The writing that the first nations didnt kill wolves universally as some sort of enlightened harmony mindset does smack of this to a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T17:38:19-07:00","id":1541714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541697#post1541697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmm bear with me because I'm a brit so my experience is minimal but I've been told a lot of white writers put first nation groups on a pedestal as somehow more in tune with nature as opposed to the eco-social ramifications of high population density and feudal/early era economics. The writing that the first nations didnt kill wolves universally as some sort of enlightened harmony mindset does smack of this to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The people who told you that exaggerated things---a lot. Yes, it's true that people exaggerated the degree to which Native American cultures didn't damage the environment. But if you do even the slightest reading into the relevant literature it's very clear that there was an ideological component to environmental destruction, and that wasn't universally shared. This is true even of groups that had lifestyles where conflict with wolves would be an issue. <a href=\"https://escholarship.org/content/qt07x7c46v/qt07x7c46v_noSplash_7d38209a8a510eebcac802f398020d57.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">The Navajo were sheep herders for much of their history, but based on what records survive it appears there was not substantial conflict with wolves until deer were nearly extirpated on the Navajo reservation and the wolves started eating livestock <i>en masse</i></a>. In <i>Wolves: Behavior, Ecology, and Conservation</i>, Steven Fritts and their coauthors note that despite indigenous foragers competing with wolves for game, there still wasn't much conflict with the species. And they're not idealizing Native Americans; they note that there was killing of pups. It just seems to have been sporadic and localized rather than a large-scale campaign.<br /> <br /> In contrast, by the point at which the Navajo started persecuting wolves (mid-1900s), the total extermination of wolves had been an official government fixation in the USA for many years and wolves had been exterminated in several European countries for centuries. Since the Middle Ages it had been seen as evil in much of Europe. Even in natural history books, such as <i>The Natural History of Quadrupeds</i>, you'd get quotes like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wolves are such ferocious and useless creatures that all other animals detest them, yea they even hate each other, and therefore scarcely ever live together, each one in its own separate hole. [...] Perhaps of all other animals, wolves are the most hateful while living and the most useless when dead. [...] The continual agitations of this restless animal renders him os furious, that he frequently ends his life in madness. </div> </div> </div>And while unfortunately I can't find my copy of <i>The Nature of Tomorrow: A History of the Environmental Future</i> right now, in it Rawson talks a lot about utopian visions of the future after the early modern period, exterminating all other forms of life was seen as a positive good.<br /> <br /> It's kind of hard to read the scholarly literature on this subject and not come to the conclusion that for much of its history, most of Europe was simply unusually bad. It's not that Native Americans were perfectly in touch with nature, it's that much of Europe had a sociopathic disregard for other forms of life and a level of wolf-hatred that is best referred to as &quot;psychotic.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T20:18:03-07:00","id":1541721,"title":"","content":"That really shouldn't come as much of a surprise; a notable amount of the push back against environmental action comes from Christians with that kind of attitude. If they're not denouncing it as some kind of idol worship (because if you treat anything but church as important, apparently, that's an idol), they're arguing that god needs to destroy the world or that god wouldn't let it run out of resources (different people, different flavors of appalling ideas). Turns out that an apocalyptic cult that's primarily concerned with taking over the world from the Romans might not be so great at keeping parts of said world around for future generations, because they frequently believe that there won't be any, even though the dust has cleared time and again and, lo and behold, the world has not ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T00:07:35-07:00","id":1541724,"title":"","content":"In Finnish, words for wolf also mean bad things. Luckily NOT curse words, but still. And I have an old (from the 1950s) zoology book that states wolves are the lead cause of caribou loss.<br /> <br /> Okay, Jukka.<br /> <br /> I do find it interesting how wolves got the negative label because in the bible wolves are mentioned rarely while dogs are the resident evil canid. I wonder if it had to do with early Christians disliking Rome's origin story related to the she-wolf? Though I do know here up north (especially in Finland and Russia) wolves rarely were seen as positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T01:09:50-07:00","id":1541725,"title":"","content":"We usually shoot all wolves near my village and the surrounding woods last time I visited them in Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T10:55:03-07:00","id":1541743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541724#post1541724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Finnish, words for wolf also mean bad things. Luckily NOT curse words, but still. And I have an old (from the 1950s) zoology book that states wolves are the lead cause of caribou loss.<br /> <br /> Okay, Jukka.<br /> <br /> I do find it interesting how wolves got the negative label because in the bible wolves are mentioned rarely while dogs are the resident evil canid. I wonder if it had to do with early Christians disliking Rome's origin story related to the she-wolf? Though I do know here up north (especially in Finland and Russia) wolves rarely were seen as positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dogs stuck around and, frequently abandoned, had to make a living somehow. Becoming scavengers in some locales probably didn't endear them, since it seems like scavengers always get a bad rap, even if they're actually quite sociable among their own; this is why why think of vultures as filthy and evil when they preen themselves and reportedly have the mannerisms and demeanor of housecats, and of course, humans have been piling shit on hyenas for ages, from ancient folklore to Gary Gygax being an asshole about gnolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T11:22:27-07:00","id":1541744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541743#post1541743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dogs stuck around and, frequently abandoned, had to make a living somehow. Becoming scavengers in some locales probably didn't endear them, since it seems like scavengers always get a bad rap, even if they're actually quite sociable among their own; this is why why think of vultures as filthy and evil when they preen themselves and reportedly have the mannerisms and demeanor of housecats, and of course, humans have been piling shit on hyenas for ages, from ancient folklore to Gary Gygax being an asshole about gnolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just meant that for all that the bible is critical of dogs, it is wolves who ended up on the shit-list long term.<br /> <br /> Though, <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/177504879037/random-werewolf-fact-19-werewolves-vs-evil\" target=\"_blank\">werewolves ironically weren't always seen as bad.</a> It is only <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/188074828812/random-werewolf-fact-44-when-werewolves-went\" target=\"_blank\">later they got the rabid label.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T11:37:35-07:00","id":1541745,"title":"","content":"There was also the tale of Bisclavret, too, where being a werewolf apparently wasn't mentioned as a knock against the main character at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T12:27:22-07:00","id":1541747,"title":"","content":"Old Trucker is the only Native American person in the book, I think. I can't think of anyone other than him. Because I've been mulling over the way the event of the follow-up to Abbie getting killed by vampires is described on pg 85 in an email:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We\u2019re doing it.<br /> <br /> We need to be full pack for this one. Bring blades. Make sure Yuga isn\u2019t packing. Plus, one spotter with the tranq.<br /> <br /> Yuga IS gonna lose it, so this message is not for him. Control him. Just say this war is payback for Abbie. He\u2019ll buy it. Partial truth. I talked to Old Trucker about the city, the leeches. Apparently this ain\u2019t the first time the packs of the nation rage across downtown Chicago.<br /> <br /> Trucker was like, \u201cCall this Rite by a referential name, a recent name too soon lost, call this Rite the Blood Red Moon. This is a re-declaration of war. A second commencement of an original species-wide war that your generation has almost obliviated.\u201d<br /> <br /> Guess it comes down to us hating the monkeys for killing Mother so hard, so blind, we didn\u2019t see the literal undead Wyrm-beasts hiding inside some tight monkey-skin suit. Yeah, was a fucking baby dracula that killed Abbie.<br /> <br /> [ ... ]<br /> <br /> So next step is this: We do the Rite. We hope the packs nor th of Gar y hear of it and let the streets run re d. Eat dead flesh till we puke it out mixed with sc otch deep in the city as we\u2019ve ever been, all the way up in Wicker Park! But first, we do the Rite so no one doubts or chickens out.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The thing I've been mulling over: Is this section implying that summoning that Ancestor Spirit was actually a mistake and now he's this bad influence who will be leading this Pack to their death? Because after Old Trucker was summoned, things only got worse: Abbie got killed, the Ancestor Spirit convinced one Pack member to start an all-out war with all the vampires in the city, and that Pack member wants to get it done by lying to another Pack member about what's really going to happen and the entire thing rests on other nearby Garou Packs hopefully (!) backing them up... That just sounds like a recipe for disaster!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T13:37:20-07:00","id":1541748,"title":"","content":"Under A Blood Red Moon callback, is it?<br /> <br /> MAKE A PACK WHERE EVERYONE HAS A SUN WHIP<br /> [advicepuppy.jpg]<br /> NAME THEM ALL AFTER CASTLEVANIA CHARACTERS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T18:50:15-07:00","id":1541758,"title":"","content":"Baby Dracula is an IC term? That's hilarious...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T18:57:52-07:00","id":1541759,"title":"","content":"So I this isn't quite the right thread for it but if anyone got the preview chapter of WtE by subscribing to Mundus's ko-fi. Like how do a roughly 38 page preview compare to 230 ish book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T02:41:17-07:00","id":1541771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541758#post1541758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baby Dracula is an IC term? That's hilarious...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a passage where this Garou is just rambling about vampires:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Far as Old Trucker knows, the anemia banes have always been here, but us colonialist Wyrm-comers (God, I miss Abbie) have brought some really shitty ones over from the old countries. They steer shit from hiding. Illuminati is them, misunderstood. Would not bat an eye if I learned a solid 37,6% of climate change was due to their fucking centuries-long monkey-farming schemes. </div> </div> </div>Now <i>that's</i> hilarious...<br /> <br /> (Also, I wonder what the 37,6 % refers to because that's an oddly specific number.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T14:46:19-07:00","id":1541996,"title":"","content":"(&quot;Singing&quot;) Baby Dracula bluh bluh bluh blood Baby Dracula bluh bluh bluh blood...<br /> <br /> I wonder if they're going to keep that whole &quot;the Mokole culled early pre-anthropoids until tool users emerged&quot; bit of the lore. It's not like it would be out of step with the Chrono Trigger Reptoid material that Paradox was pressing in the last bits of W20 lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T01:50:59-07:00","id":1542036,"title":"","content":"Ya know if Mundus's theory that W5 as a whole is actually some massive gaslighting effort aimed at lost cubs:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can definitely see that. Even the 'twisted upbringing flaw' reflects exactly that: a Garou who was only offered a highly distorted view of the Garou and needs to undergo extensive deprogramming.<br /> <br /> Playing with the 'unreality' idea of the W5 universe crossing over to WtE, there's a Pentex version of Werewolf: the Apocalypse they put out that almost hilariously features a lot of aspects of the w5 verse. Imagine a game setting where Pentex did, in fact, release their version of Werewolf (Lycanthrope: the Rapture). Canonically it was never released, but maybe in an alt universe iIt became a household name like D&amp;D. Suddenly, you have a fuckton of Lost Cubs who believe that game world is real and begin reaching out to work with the makers (the 'fuck everyone' elders of w5) who are looking to trap the players in increasingly amoral missions until it becomes imperative for the player characters to go 'no fucking way' and start looking around themselves with the intention to see through the ruse (and you'd have to work with the players that they expect the subversion.)<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>Like it really puts the setting into context dosn't it? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T08:50:50-07:00","id":1542178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541721#post1541721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really shouldn't come as much of a surprise; a notable amount of the push back against environmental action comes from Christians with that kind of attitude. If they're not denouncing it as some kind of idol worship (because if you treat anything but church as important, apparently, that's an idol), they're arguing that god needs to destroy the world or that god wouldn't let it run out of resources (different people, different flavors of appalling ideas). Turns out that an apocalyptic cult that's primarily concerned with taking over the world from the Romans might not be so great at keeping parts of said world around for future generations, because they frequently believe that there won't be any, even though the dust has cleared time and again and, lo and behold, the world has not ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll be generations realizing just how much the GOP co-opted the Religious Right as a propaganda arm for whatever crazy idea they wanted to forward from Reagan onward. Barry Goldwater was afraid the preachers and faithful would corrupt the Right but it turned out to be a two way street ouroboros.<br /> <br /> I'm basically quoting my father here.<br /> <br /> They want to go against environmentalists, suddenly Jesus hates trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T14:16:01-07:00","id":1542394,"title":"","content":"One of the disappointing elements of W5 is that it's way too matter-of-fact in how political it is. Sure, WtA always was political. Environmentalism was only the most obvious angle in that regard. But the spiritualism and animism of WtA should be seen as an asset in approaching these political issues from a different perspective. What W5 offers instead is far more worldly and grounded in present-day activism. Even though, the religious right in the US is an interesting topic for a game like WtA. What allowed things like Mormonism to establish itself? Or since one of the core-elements of W5 is the <i>Cult </i>of Fenris, why not take a look at cults in the US like the Manson family?<br /> <br /> Or to take a WtA-specific thing: How about exploring the switch from Gaia-worship to Luna-worship by drawing parallels to the switch from polytheistic believers to Christianity, like what the Vikings went through, for example? And of course, it wasn't just about religion and a matter of faith. There's plenty to explore here that goes beyond just having the Garou be environmental activists and the bad Cult of Fenris be right-wing extremists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T18:37:16-07:00","id":1542407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542394#post1542394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the disappointing elements of W5 is that it's way too matter-of-fact in how political it is. Sure, WtA always was political. Environmentalism was only the most obvious angle in that regard. But the spiritualism and animism of WtA should be seen as an asset in approaching these political issues from a different perspective. What W5 offers instead is far more worldly and grounded in present-day activism. Even though, the religious right in the US is an interesting topic for a game like WtA. What allowed things like Mormonism to establish itself? Or since one of the core-elements of W5 is the <i>Cult </i>of Fenris, why not take a look at cults in the US like the Manson family?<br /> <br /> Or to take a WtA-specific thing: How about exploring the switch from Gaia-worship to Luna-worship by drawing parallels to the switch from polytheistic believers to Christianity, like what the Vikings went through, for example? And of course, it wasn't just about religion and a matter of faith. There's plenty to explore here that goes beyond just having the Garou be environmental activists and the bad Cult of Fenris be right-wing extremists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it is like this so it doesn't become too hard for the players to relate to the characters. Granted I don't think that is true, but it seems like W5 tries to remove as much of Garou specific issues and only focus on real world issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T19:44:22-07:00","id":1542411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542407#post1542407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel it is like this so it doesn't become too hard for the players to relate to the characters. Granted I don't think that is true, but it seems like W5 tries to remove as much of Garou specific issues and only focus on real world issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a very centrist take on RL issues at that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T09:20:35-07:00","id":1542431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542411#post1542411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And a very centrist take on RL issues at that...</div> </div> </div> </div>My definition of centrist tends more towards &quot;lacking any party identification and therefore takes heterodox positions on a variety of issues&quot; (To quote Chris Rock: &quot;I'm conservative about taxes. I'm liberal about strippers!&quot;). Which, as a political organizer, is less then ideal but at least something I can work with.<br /> <br /> What is so frustrating about W5 is that its ideology and rhetoric isn't even centrist. Its moderate. What I call &quot;the mushball moderates&quot;. Which are actually center-right leaning lovers of the status-quo. David Brooks being the perfect example. To their (upper middle class) eyes everything is fine the way it is: Nothing should change too much or too quickly. The left wing should be quickly upbraided for everything their fringe utters. Meanwhile they demand the angry fringes of the right be understood, spoken to, compromised with, and catered to. Societal others (women, POC, queers) are free to make the case for their humanity, but only if they do it the right way. Politely and in a calm measured voice (while a boot stands on their neck). Fascism is a historical boogeyman we defeated in WWII so why are you bringing it up now?<br /> <br /> Whatever your politics (and I obviously wear mine on my sleeve) we can agree that OG W:tA was possessed a deeply radical politics. Radical as in &quot;relating to or addressing the the root (causes)&quot;. Eco-Terrorism and/or spiritual warfare against the wyrm are deeply radical projects. Even the spirituality and social context is radical, weather it be an exploration of animism (often disparaged to as a &quot;primitive&quot; religion or worldview) or communal living in an (idealized) tribal arrangement.<br /> <br /> And W5 just seems uninterested in any of that. Some of the toning down is understandable at least. The Chechnya kerfuffle surely had caused some harsh edges to be sanded off. And its understandable now in 2024 the responsible position is to be a LOT less cavalier about political violence. But I still expected some sort of motive force, some sort of directionality or position that could frame the action. Like, you can retain an agnostic position in the game text regarding &quot;Garou must return to the old was VS the old ways must be left behind or destroyed&quot; and just present it as a conflict in the setting. But we don't get that because no one remembers the lore, the elders are all dead, and oral history degrades SUPER fast evidently. Or a conflict like &quot;KILL PENTEX REND SHRED BITE VS &quot;actually some people who work in that Megadon front office are nice normal people who just want a paycheck and also volunteer at a homeless shelter on the weekends&quot;. Except no, because all the subsidiaries are gone and incremental change is the best you can hope for.<br /> <br /> This is the definition of a &quot;me&quot; problem but I do not want to play &quot;Union Organizer: The Card Checking&quot; in my free time.<br /> <br /> So you have a game that incorporates drama. Both games and drama almost require conflict (or at least competition, a form of conflict). When the ideology of your games presupposes the primacy of the status quo and the shushing of anything more radical than another cut in the capital gains tax you're left with a game without a conflict. So you're left with something that not only feels apolitical but devoid of stimulus to act in any direction. Nothing is incentivized, everything is punished. Action is a sin and ambition is unseemly. And that's why I think even those who don't share my politics find something lacking in W5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T11:19:12-07:00","id":1542434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcusVitel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542431#post1542431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we don't get that because no one remembers the lore, the elders are all dead, and oral history degrades SUPER fast evidently. Or a conflict like &quot;KILL PENTEX REND SHRED BITE VS &quot;actually some people who work in that Megadon front office are nice normal people who just want a paycheck and also volunteer at a homeless shelter on the weekends&quot;. Except no, because all the subsidiaries are gone and incremental change is the best you can hope for.<br /> <br /> This is the definition of a &quot;me&quot; problem but I do not want to play &quot;Union Organizer: The Card Checking&quot; in my free time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the way the environmental organization is depicted, too. Literally only good for distractions and there is no mention of any actual effect they have. Which to me is the most telling aspect of this. It is saying it is pointless to try and those who do are all extremists.<br /> <br /> It wants to continue the theme, but W5 is too afraid of having their characters actually committing crimes/terrorism to push it. Even though, the alternative is this; Union the Card Checking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T12:59:53-07:00","id":1542435,"title":"","content":"The lack of commitment to any political perspective is part of a bigger issue that has been plaguing W5 as a whole: It's shallow. And it becomes very apparent whenever the rubber meets the road in terms of worldbuilding, setting-description and any other sort of detail that tries to make sense of what is being described.<br /> <br /> To focus on one part in particular: diversity. W5 has this idea of a fallen Garou Nation where regional traditions and beliefs are very important to Garou as references for their Rites and norms. Like when it says on pg 7 &quot;Modern communications technology means that Garou can talk to each other easier than ever before, and so have realized that their immutable traditions and culture are often actually entirely local. Other Garou in other places do things differently.&quot;. But W5 is having a hard time putting this into action and follow up on this premise in a meaningful way.<br /> <br /> The reason: W5 seems to be deathly afraid of paying attention to any tradition, people, culture or region outside of North America and Europe for more than a nanosecond. (Then again, W5's relationship with Native American culture isn't faring that much better either...)<br /> <br /> Take a description like the one for Princess Mari from the Sept of the North Country: &quot;An eighteen-year-old Lebanese teenager from New York found by a pack still loyal to Albrecht. She used to have another name and another family, but after her First Change, she was brought here and renamed after an old packmate of the King.\u200b&quot; Why Lebanese...? It often feels like these references like someone being from somewhere outside North America and Europe are made to simply make it <i>seem </i>like this book cares about any setting outside of Europe and North America. You get things like a Chinese Taikonaut, someone from Nigeria or India or you have a Sept that is rescuing Libyan refugees in the Mediterranean. All of these references are presented with the depth of a puddle, though. Scratch the surface and the references come off as almost random for how little they seem to matter in the writing. There's never any deeper meaning or consideration here. The country-names get invoked as &quot;other&quot; and &quot;not-Europe/North-America&quot; but that's about it. In the case of the section for the Sept of the Water's Birth Libya might as well be just a black hole that people are fleeing from. Or take a look at how you have this one Loresheet for this one Chinese Taikonaut who has a special relationship with Luna. There's no depth to making that character Chinese. It might as well be just a random name of space-faring nations drawn out of a hat.<br /> <br /> And to further highlight W5's absolute focus on North America and Europe, let's just ponder why this book felt the need to include this sentence on Liu Aihan's character-sheet: &quot;When off-duty from the space program, she travels the world, teaching other Garou about Luna and how they can shed the limits of their auspices.\u200b&quot; Could it maybe be because there's an unwritten rule in W5 that adventures outside of North America and Europe are somehow unimaginable for W5's official products...?<br /> <br /> The closest this book gets to having something that isn't about Europe or North America is the Legendary Rite about Ross the She-Wolf taking on Union Bromide. But the writing is so bland that there's little reason for why the setting couldn't just be &quot;Insert random country with a Supreme Court here&quot;. The descriptions and worldbuilding are simply so uninvolved and meaningless that the &quot;where&quot; of the whole scenario could pretty much be characterized as &quot;anywhere&quot;.<br /> <br /> And this shallowness is such a big problem because it has now repeatedly led to writing where it feels like you're getting a half-formed idea - and right there the thinking starts and ends. It never feels like the ideas are explored to a degree where you get something that inspires the imagination or illuminates a particular setting in a meaningful way. It's just this series of signposts gesturing at various things. Saving Libyan refugees from the Mediterranean? Sure, why not? Protecting environmental activists from bad guys? Okay, that sounds right. Sabotaging an Amazon warehouse? Certainly sucks to work there! Add it to the list! But all of this... It's about as meaningful as McDonalds tweeting &quot;BlackLivesMatter&quot;. It's shallow. W5 is more concerned with what activism looks like than delving into the why of it all.<br /> <br /> But of course, that's hard to do when W5 still falls into tropes like making Europe and North America the center of attention while everything else on the globe is just a sideshow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T23:20:14-07:00","id":1542475,"title":"","content":"So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> I've found this video that on arknights (a tower defence gacha game) lore kinda relates to Albrecht and W5 as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Filg0MkpCrk?si=g8EQqgLhMo7a4zki\" data-code=\"Filg0MkpCrk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Filg0MkpCrk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> To heavy summarise the video centres around a man called Mlynar who like Albrecht has shown to have grew disisslulisoned with his cause (kinghthood in Mlynar's case) and has all but given up on said cause. And like Albrecht he's content on strew in his own misery and not doing anything to change the current satius quoe. Of course Mlynar unlike Albrecht actually started to change partly due to the efforts of his nieces. Like could you even picture W5 Albrecht leading a leagon of kinghts to the defence of his homeland from capitalism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T11:03:25-07:00","id":1542561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542475#post1542475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> I've found this video that on arknights (a tower defence gacha game) lore kinda relates to Albrecht and W5 as a whole.<br /> <br /> To heavy summarise the video centres around a man called Mlynar who like Albrecht has shown to have grew disisslulisoned with his cause (kinghthood in Mlynar's case) and has all but given up on said cause. And like Albrecht he's content on strew in his own misery and not doing anything to change the current satius quoe. Of course Mlynar unlike Albrecht actually started to change partly due to the efforts of his nieces. Like could you even picture W5 Albrecht leading a leagon of kinghts to the defence of his homeland from capitalism?</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept you mention is fine. It's the way it's presented that makes it bad. In my review, I call Shattered-Nation-Albrecht a &quot;cranky, self-important old man&quot;. That's the issue. On one hand, it explains why this version of the character was involved in the fall of the Garou-Nation but on the other hand, it's hard to imagine this character being the king to begin with or be the same Albrecht from previous editions (despite the obvious reference that's made here).<br /> <br /> Here's another part of how Shattered Nation presents Albrecht (this was another official preview for the book): <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1243\" height=\"795\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cHK9JgE.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cHK9JgE.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/cHK9JgE.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> This &quot;he's too impatient due to Rage and just stormed off during the Rite&quot;... To me, the Albrecht in this section, in particular, reads less like a disillusioned, tragic hero and more like the idea of an incompetent king with grandiose ambitions and a lot of delusions finally coming to terms with how the whole Garou Nation has fallen apart around him. The Albrecht from this book is a king who hasn't been up to the task and his character flaws were just the icing on the cake for the flailing Garou Nation that ultimately failed during his reign.<br /> <br /> Strangely, though, one of the Legendary Rites is the Morningkill-stuff and the search for the Silver Crown from the legacy-editions. But that idea of Albrecht isn't anywhere else in the book. It's only in that Legendary Rite that you get a glimpse of how Albrecht was portrayed in previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T11:54:29-07:00","id":1542567,"title":"","content":"They're not even keying off the whole secret curse of Luna from SF Revised, are they? Or even that Albrecht was supposed to, you know, die in the plotlines from Rev...<br /> <br /> Oh, silly me. Thinking that they might incorporate something from as recent as when I, a past-40 millennial, <i>was in high school</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:52:21-07:00","id":1542576,"title":"","content":"To mention another thing about Albrecht in this book: One of the odder elements of the book regarding Albrecht is the Legendary Rite called &quot;The Final Battle&quot;. This is how it's described:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the Umbra, legends live forever. So it was that King Jonas Albrecht led his tribe and many famous Garou to battle the forces of the Wyrm during the Apocalypse. They encountered their nemeses, Margrave Yuri Konietzko and Tamara Tvarivich, and their combined forces, all sworn to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Albrecht fought the Wyrm\u2019s forces, but when Zhyzhak arrived with Wyrm itself, the Garou went berserk and attacked their King instead. Jonas Albrecht, mortally wounded, managed to use his Silver Crown to kill Zhyzhak, but in doing so, destroyed the crown.<br /> <br /> Collapsing from his wounds, he managed to escape the Umbra, broken and barely alive. Thus, the Garou Nation and Jonas Albrecht were shattered. </div> </div> </div>There isn't even a real story attached to this. It's just fighting, fighting, fighting and then either Albrecht (or the Garou who &quot;plays&quot; him in the Rite, I guess) survives or not. And what are people not familiar with the legacy-material even supposed to think when names like the &quot;Margrave&quot;, for example, are invoked...?<br /> <br /> Just really odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T16:01:16-07:00","id":1542588,"title":"","content":"Was looking in SF Revised for a different reason, but came across the vision that Albrecht had just to be able to claim the crown. It is entirely contra to everything that happens in the above quote. That's not even getting into the &quot;Whoops, all the other characters in leadership positions are actually corrupt!&quot; factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T16:54:12-07:00","id":1542594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542576#post1542576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To mention another thing about Albrecht in this book: One of the odder elements of the book regarding Albrecht is the Legendary Rite called &quot;The Final Battle&quot;. This is how it's described:<br /> <br /> <br /> There isn't even a real story attached to this. It's just fighting, fighting, fighting and then either Albrecht (or the Garou who &quot;plays&quot; him in the Rite, I guess) survives or not. And what are people not familiar with the legacy-material even supposed to think when names like the &quot;Margrave&quot;, for example, are invoked...?<br /> <br /> Just really odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand why they need to be so spiteful with the Legacy.<br /> <br /> In the Last Battle novel, Magrave died in the realm of the Apocalypse. Meanwhile Albrecht and the rest gathered their forces into a circular mountain range with only one opening for the Wyrm's forces to come through. The Perfect Crinos-born took the crown from Alby and decided to do Wyrmt things, until he realised he was in the wrong and gave it back, dying in the process.<br /> <br /> Alby then asked to crown for one last burst of energy, which he used to kill Zhyzhak.<br /> <br /> (Also you can't bring the Wyrm to a battle, it would be like if you brought Gravity to a fight.)<br /> <br /> This spiteful retelling also ignores one glaring issue; If Zhyzhak won, why aren't the BSDs running rampant and openly doing their deeds? Why aren't they the face of WoD 5's werewolves?<br /> <br /> The answer is, of course, that Zhyzhak doesn't matter. The point of this retelling is to put the NPCs of the Legacy down. Yes, this could be a case of 'oral history is not accurate', but it brings up concepts that aren't actually present in W5. In the same book, BSDs are portrayed as chill and more likely to listen than the CoF. That is not a tribe Zhyzhak comes from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T18:17:51-07:00","id":1542598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542561#post1542561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The concept you mention is fine. It's the way it's presented that makes it bad. In my review, I call Shattered-Nation-Albrecht a &quot;cranky, self-important old man&quot;. That's the issue. On one hand, it explains why this version of the character was involved in the fall of the Garou-Nation but on the other hand, it's hard to imagine this character being the king to begin with or be the same Albrecht from previous editions (despite the obvious reference that's made here).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the bolded is basically Mlynar's initial characterisation. Like the scene the audience seen of him is him scolding his nice for daring to participate in the Kazimierz Major and tainting they family name by associating with the event that in his view marks the death of knighthood rather than letting it fade away, before promptly slinking away after getting a call from his boss. Which give an audience the impression that he's a spineless hypocrite, welling to call out all the injustice in the system but quickly fall in line as soon as own his livelihood is on the line.<br /> <br /> Of course unlike Albrecht Mlynar did regain the will to be a hero. Partly thanks to a support network that W5 Albrecht lacks. From his both nieces who despite putting up with his fowl attitude still empathise some of his points which drives them to participate in the Kazimierz Major to show the citizens the meaning of true knighthood rather than do nothing, the Sliver Lance Pegisi a order of knights who still believes in Mlynar's potential to be a hero despite his clams to the contrary and his own friend Toland who promptly calls Mlynar out for being a miserable fart and informing him of a faction of Kazimierz government is planning a purge a slum, which Mlynar promptly (if reluctly) stops because he's still a hero.<br /> <br /> This all culminates in Mlynar finally giving cashing in three months of paid leave form his job and lead the Sliver Lance Pegisi to save his family from being assassinated, then finally interesting his older niece Nearl to guide the future of Kazimierz knights before going on his own quests.<br /> <br /> <br /> And You know the players deciding to form a support network for Albrecht and help him rekindle his will to lead the garou is a neat idea for an adventure...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542594#post1542594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Last Battle novel, Magrave died in the realm of the Apocalypse. Meanwhile Albrecht and the rest gathered their forces into a circular mountain range with only one opening for the Wyrm's forces to come through. The Perfect Crinos-born took the crown from Alby and decided to do Wyrmt things, until he realised he was in the wrong and gave it back, dying in the process.<br /> <br /> Alby then asked to crown for one last burst of energy, which he used to kill Zhyzhak.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also in WtE Albrecht trapped himself and storm eater in the deep umbra. Implicitly if not stopping the Apocalypse then at least buying the fera valuable time.to come up with some silution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542594#post1542594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why they need to be so spiteful with the Legacy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to think if W5 is a Matrix like situation and in universe Spite is the point. And Albrecht condition is basically the end goal of the big bad of \u200bMatrix Resurrections for Neo (which is to reduce him to broken self loathing shell of a man) and undoubtably Storm Eater is gonna have plenty of spite for the man who deny his destruction of the world...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 09-24-2024, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T22:56:21-07:00","id":1542610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542594#post1542594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand why they need to be so spiteful with the Legacy.<br /> <br /> In the Last Battle novel, Magrave died in the realm of the Apocalypse. Meanwhile Albrecht and the rest gathered their forces into a circular mountain range with only one opening for the Wyrm's forces to come through. The Perfect Crinos-born took the crown from Alby and decided to do Wyrmt things, until he realised he was in the wrong and gave it back, dying in the process.<br /> <br /> Alby then asked to crown for one last burst of energy, which he used to kill Zhyzhak.<br /> <br /> (Also you can't bring the Wyrm to a battle, it would be like if you brought Gravity to a fight.)<br /> <br /> This spiteful retelling also ignores one glaring issue; If Zhyzhak won, why aren't the BSDs running rampant and openly doing their deeds? Why aren't they the face of WoD 5's werewolves?<br /> <br /> The answer is, of course, that Zhyzhak doesn't matter. The point of this retelling is to put the NPCs of the Legacy down. Yes, this could be a case of 'oral history is not accurate', but it brings up concepts that aren't actually present in W5. In the same book, BSDs are portrayed as chill and more likely to listen than the CoF. That is not a tribe Zhyzhak comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That they killed Zhyzhak, it's literally written in the except quoted by Knightingale. It's Just that Albrecht came out severely wounded and with a broken Army afterwards.<br /> <br /> Also, a minor nitpick: that in old good days before W5 you could and should actually fight the Wyrm as an existing Monster (instead of doing hoomie thingies) is a frequent criticism against W5 \ud83d\ude03","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T23:50:42-07:00","id":1542615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542610#post1542610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That they killed Zhyzhak, it's literally written in the except quoted by Knightingale. It's Just that Albrecht came out severely wounded and with a broken Army afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, missed that. Thank you for correcting me. The matter still stands, however, that the Nation fell and BSDs are still around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542610#post1542610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a minor nitpick: that in old good days before W5 you could and should actually fight the Wyrm as an existing Monster (instead of doing hoomie thingies) is a frequent criticism against W5 \ud83d\ude03</div> </div> </div> </div>You could never fight the Wyrm physically, You could fight its minions. But Wyrm itself is basically like gravity, a force of nature. Zhyzhak could not bring it to the battlefield any more than one can bring the wind itself to a battlefield. You can bring aspects, but never the actual whole monty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T04:25:40-07:00","id":1542620,"title":"","content":"In regards to the Legendary Rites, there are these sidebars where Dominique &quot;Death-In-Word&quot; Omar (the Silver Fang Ragabash) and Little Sister (the Children of Gaia Philodox) talk with each other about these Rites. And it's made clear that Dominique isn't trying to portray historical truths in those Legendary Rites. For example, in the section for &quot;The Quest for the Silver Crown&quot;, the sidebar says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Queen Morningkill<br /> Dominique \u201cDeath-in-Word\u201d Omar: We\u2019ll need someone for the role of Queen Morningkill. Who wants to get assassinated?<br /> Little Sister: Wait, \u2019Queen Morningkill\u2019? I thought it was King Morningkill, Albrecht\u2019s father, who was killed?<br /> Dominique \u201cDeath-in-Word\u201d Omar: Who\u2019s running this Rite? You or me?<br /> Little Sister: You.<br /> Dominique \u201cDeath-in-Word\u201d Omar: That\u2019s right. If I make her into a queen, she\u2019ll be a queen. </div> </div> </div>And you have another one of those for &quot;The Last Battle&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Riding the Wyrm<br /> Little Sister: Wow, the Wyrm was there? Like, in person?<br /> Dominique \u201cDeath-in-Word\u201d Omar: Sure, of course. King Albrecht defeated it, and we all lived happily ever after.<br /> Little Sister: But\u2014<br /> Dominique \u201cDeath-in-Word\u201d Omar: If you ever become the topic of a Legendary Rite, I\u2019ll make sure you\u2019ll be riding a dragon and waving a sword twice your size.<br /> Little Sister: I don\u2019t think I\u2019d ever be the subject of a story like that.<br /> Dominique \u201cDeath-in-Word\u201d Omar: That\u2019s not typically for you to decide. These Rites are created by those who come after.\u200b </div> </div> </div>And there's a discussion about &quot;making changes&quot; on pg. 106 where it says &quot;You can remind the players that their characters change the Rite if they so choose. They can shift the story or adjust their roles, but these are in-game choices. Storyteller characters know the Rite as it\u2019s usually performed and notice adjustments. Whether they like them or not depend on how well the players\u2019 characters pull them off. If the character playing the villain throws the fight and loses on purpose, that\u2019s generally considered inauspicious. What\u2019s the point of winning a fight when there\u2019s no resistance?\u200b&quot; So, changes like genderswapping or changing the location make sense to me. For example, you genderswap a role depending who's performing what role in the Legendary Rite. Or the Legendary Rite is performed at a Sept in Alaska but the location of the story is the Sahara Desert. And so the location gets switched to some arctic ice-wasteland. Or the Legendary Rite tells a story from over two hundred years ago but you decide to modernize the references and tell the story as if it had happened last year.<br /> <br /> I wonder how others interpret this but the sidebar for the &quot;Last Battle&quot;-Legendary Rite made me think, though, that it's implied that the source for this Legendary Rite was Dominique simply making shit up. And I think there should be limits to how much of a Legendary Rite can be just fiction invented by a participant. For example, it should be against Garou society norms to do the &quot;Quest for the Silver Crown&quot; Legendary Rite and add a bit about how Albrecht got rejected by the Silver Crown and so he secretly made a fake-replica of the Silver Crown and proclaimed himself to be king anyway. There should be huge repercussions for doing something like that, both in terms of Renown and how both Garou and Spirits interact with a Garou who did something like that. In the same way, you shouldn't be able to do a Legendary Rite, take a well-known Garou-hero of the past and claim that they actually sided with the Wyrm during a big battle.<br /> <br /> A Legendary Rite should be more than just doing an avant-garde local theater production at a Sept and it shouldn't be considered an opportunity to write fan-fiction about the past. It's a Rite after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T06:14:24-07:00","id":1542624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542620#post1542620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I just realised that legendary rites are actually ripoof of the Heroquests from the Glorantha setting in the senes that people are assigned to role play mythic events of the past to boost they abilities.<br /> <br /> Of course Heroquests have extremely stringent requirments that must be followed. Mainly the person playing it must actually be a follower of the figure (whose usally a god) and they mustn't divert from the script or terrible consequences will ensure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T10:25:24-07:00","id":1542635,"title":"","content":"Legendary Rites: Because we didn't want anyone to remember the Legendary Realm. Or any Near Realms, or that Near Realms were a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T14:44:55-07:00","id":1542647,"title":"","content":"I do think that the Legendary Rites are pretty cool. Using them as an inspiration for stuff to do at moots, rites in general, and a grab bag of archetypal stories that one can use for a stuff in Werewolf is something that I\u2019ll probably try to adapt for my own use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T23:59:50-07:00","id":1542669,"title":"","content":"I am not familiar with W5 or Legendary Rites, but the idea of people are assigned to role play mythic events of the past sounds very much like the fourth level Galliard Gift Shadows by the Firelight.<br /> <br /> It is one of those Gifts I always thought should play an important part in a chronicle, but the lack of support for it kneecapped it. You really need a dozen or so legends, summarized in a paragraph or so, at hand for an ST to have at hand to use and serve as an inspiration to brainstorm more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T02:04:59-07:00","id":1542671,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on Legendary Rites:<ul><li>At one point, it talks about Sept-politics in the sense that Garou with one point of view took on the role of the good guys and the Garou who opposed their perspective then chose to take on the role of the villain. So on one level, you're playing out a story but on another level, this is a way to hash out differences in a Sept. Legendary Rites could be interesting in that regard.</li> <li>It's also mentioned that playing the roles in the Legendary Rite attracts the attention of Spirits. For example, in the &quot;Last Battle&quot;-example, it says &quot;This is a tragedy where we know the hero will fail. Most characters will be playing Wyrm entities or Garou possessed by them, but the magic of the Legendary Rite protects them from actually being possessed by Banes. At least, it should.&quot; I think you could go further by having Spirits help Garou play their respective roles. And this includes Bane-Spirits helping the ones who play villainous roles. The book doesn't go too deep into what this exactly means but I think this would also add some nuance to this whole thing. The role a Garou is playing isn't just there for individualistic artistic expression. And when you're playing a Black Spiral Dancer in a Legendary Rite, as far as the Spirits are concerned, you are a Black Spiral Dancer for the duration of this Rite. I think there's lots to explore there when you look at Legendary Rites as these mystical affairs that attract the attention of all sorts of Spirits.</li> </ul>Where the book falters a bit:<ul><li>If we imagine that the average table has an ST and three to four players, it's strange that three of the four example Legendary Rites have five named roles attached to them. And in those three cases, it's also five named characters <i>plus </i>indistinct groups of background-actors that should also be there like &quot;Albrecht's packmates&quot; or &quot;Black Spiral Dancers&quot;. That's why I thought of LARP. Once you're juggling those types of numbers, a LARP would be the perfect setting for something like these Legendary Rites. It's just that the book offers little in terms of support for the scenario where it is just the ST and three players. Sure, you could get the players to take on multiple roles, for example, but that's then yet another hurdle to get buy-in from the players to play out these Legendary Rites.</li> <li>This is also the same book that doubles down on Garou not knowing a lot about their history. So, that kneecaps the whole idea if part of the setting is supposed to be that Garou know very little about their past and the 80s and 90s are already &quot;ancient history&quot; as far as the Garou are concerned.</li> <li>The examples also lack variety in that they're all about a specific named Garou doing something. They are all retellings of a particular Garou's exploits. There's a lot more variety in what sorts of stories you could tell. Myths, legends... that sort of thing with more archetypical roles rather than specific named Garou, for example.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T05:36:17-07:00","id":1542678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542671#post1542671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on Legendary Rites:<br /> Snip[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if you want to expand Legendary Rites you can just steal some concepts from Heroquests from Glorantha. Like Heroquests are significant things in the setting that must be preformed in a specific time and place with very pretuclar requirements for the cast depending on the quest and most importantly the fact that they must follow the &quot;script&quot; else the quest will fail. So vluabe in fact that knowledge of a myth that might be subject of a hero quest is a valuable bargaining chip in intertribal meeting in the setting.<br /> <br /> And even with all that preparation, a hero questor is still at the risk of death or worse during a Heroquest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T12:55:36-07:00","id":1542713,"title":"","content":"I think my main hangup with Legendary Rites is it takes FAR, FAR more DNA from ' Theatre Kids do Nordic LARP' than it does from how important Dreamings, Ancestor Stories and Griotcraft are passed on and comes off as deeply artificial as a result.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 09-27-2024, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T13:55:15-07:00","id":1542714,"title":"","content":"So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> if w5 is revealed to actually matrix like situation how would react.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T07:32:44-07:00","id":1542771,"title":"","content":"My opinion on W5 is very cynical but not in the usual way.<br /> <br /> My opinion? &quot;It's just Mage Revised 2.0. The game says fighting the Technocracy was always stupid and you should be making sustainable farming with Life magic instead. However, fans still note that the Technocracy is a bunch of psychos and want to kill them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T08:37:02-07:00","id":1542780,"title":"","content":"I suppose if &quot;make shit up or change the story if you feel like it&quot; is standard practice among modern Garou, it makes sense why none of them can remember anything. Part of the way oral traditions survived was ensuring that they were retold accurately. It's not that they never changed, because of course they did, but there was still a commitment to accuracy. Meanwhile, here's Dominique just changing the story because they think it's neat.<br /> <br /> Why do none of the Garou know when the Garou Nation collapsed? Because their Galliards keep changing the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T11:20:36-07:00","id":1542785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542771#post1542771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion on W5 is very cynical but not in the usual way.<br /> <br /> My opinion? &quot;It's just Mage Revised 2.0. The game says fighting the Technocracy was always stupid and you should be making sustainable farming with Life magic instead. However, fans still note that the Technocracy is a bunch of psychos and want to kill them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In favor of Mage Revised, at least most of the mechanics still support other play styles, even the ones being actively discouraged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T14:40:49-07:00","id":1542800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542780#post1542780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose if &quot;make shit up or change the story if you feel like it&quot; is standard practice among modern Garou, it makes sense why none of them can remember anything. Part of the way oral traditions survived was ensuring that they were retold accurately. It's not that they never changed, because of course they did, but there was still a commitment to accuracy. Meanwhile, here's Dominique just changing the story because they think it's neat.<br /> <br /> Why do none of the Garou know when the Garou Nation collapsed? Because their Galliards keep changing the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to be generous, which admittedly I doubt most of us are inclined to be, you can say the problem isn't that oral tradition is being screwed up by errors.<br /> <br /> It's the fact the original stories are bullshit.<br /> <br /> You have a perfectly retold, 10,000 year old story of the War of Rage....which 100% confirms that the Gurahl deserved to die and every single other Shifter race was evil.<br /> <br /> Just because the stories are uncorrupted doesn't mean they're not originally propaganda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T14:58:45-07:00","id":1542801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542800#post1542800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you wanted to be generous, which admittedly I doubt most of us are inclined to be, you can say the problem isn't that oral tradition is being screwed up by errors.<br /> <br /> It's the fact the original stories are bullshit.<br /> <br /> You have a perfectly retold, 10,000 year old story of the War of Rage....which 100% confirms that the Gurahl deserved to die and every single other Shifter race was evil.<br /> <br /> Just because the stories are uncorrupted doesn't mean they're not originally propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you had that, the story would still be preserved. You'd have some idea that the War of Rage happened, when it happened, and some of the major events. This... this is the End of History. Not because nothing more is happening, but because the Garou intentionally destroyed their way of remembering the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T15:09:00-07:00","id":1542803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542801#post1542801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you had that, the story would still be preserved. You'd have some idea that the War of Rage happened, when it happened, and some of the major events. This... this is the End of History. Not because nothing more is happening, but because the Garou intentionally destroyed their way of remembering the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you have a story.<br /> <br /> Which isn't necessarily something any Garou is inclined to believe is true and may be a lie. Which is my point. It's a perfectly valid means of preserving information but that information does not need to be correct.<br /> <br /> The End of History is discovering yes, that the Get of Fenris were not justified in massacring the native tribal people of the New World.<br /> <br /> That the War of Rage happened but as a brutal set of atrocities.<br /> <br /> That the Impergium was, yes, wrong.<br /> <br /> Which again, is a very generous interpretation of things but nicely points out that the issue is not, &quot;Oral History is wrong&quot;, it is, &quot;The Garou are full of themselves and have deliberately refused to accept any alternative POVs or challenges to their supremacy.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T15:30:37-07:00","id":1542804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542803#post1542803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you have a story.<br /> <br /> Which isn't necessarily something any Garou is inclined to believe is true and may be a lie. Which is my point. It's a perfectly valid means of preserving information but that information does not need to be correct.<br /> <br /> The End of History is discovering yes, that the Get of Fenris were not justified in massacring the native tribal people of the New World.<br /> <br /> That the War of Rage happened but as a brutal set of atrocities.<br /> <br /> That the Impergium was, yes, wrong.<br /> <br /> Which again, is a very generous interpretation of things but nicely points out that the issue is not, &quot;Oral History is wrong&quot;, it is, &quot;The Garou are full of themselves and have deliberately refused to accept any alternative POVs or challenges to their supremacy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is actually supported by the excerpts I've seen, which don't depict this as a matter of alternate perspectives (we'd already seen plenty in Revised) but as the past being a muddled mess where even basic historical facts can't be agreed on. That's not how actual historical revisionism works in real life; I know, I've <i>read</i> it. I am proposing that an approach to oral tradition that swaps around characters and makes up details because &quot;I'm the one running this rite, I say it happened like this&quot; would be why the Garou have lost their history. I don't understand what you're trying to argue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T16:09:58-07:00","id":1542805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542803#post1542803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you have a story.<br /> <br /> Which isn't necessarily something any Garou is inclined to believe is true and may be a lie. Which is my point. It's a perfectly valid means of preserving information but that information does not need to be correct.<br /> <br /> The End of History is discovering yes, that the Get of Fenris were not justified in massacring the native tribal people of the New World.<br /> <br /> That the War of Rage happened but as a brutal set of atrocities.<br /> <br /> That the Impergium was, yes, wrong.<br /> <br /> Which again, is a very generous interpretation of things but nicely points out that the issue is not, &quot;Oral History is wrong&quot;, it is, &quot;The Garou are full of themselves and have deliberately refused to accept any alternative POVs or challenges to their supremacy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can do that. The whole &quot;history is written by the victors&quot; kind of thing. But I think you've already put way more thought into this than the Shattered Nation book has.<br /> <br /> The first Legendary Rite example is &quot;Ross the She-Wolf Fights Union Bromide&quot; and it's Ross fighting this Pentex-front. That's it. No nuance whatsoever. It's an event that happened, the Legendary Rite is just a point-by-point reproduction of that adventure and then later you get a Loresheet for Ross the She-Wolf as a good character PCs should associate with. And then when there's a sidebar, it's heavily implied that it's all coming from Dominique. And there's no Dominique/Little Sister sidebar for the &quot;Tale of the Storm Eater&quot; either, for example.<br /> <br /> I mean, you're right: Legendary Rites would be a good vehicle to make sense of how Garou look at their own history in W5 and how it could reflect on how so much historical knowledge was lost by the Garou over the centuries. Sadly, this book doesn't have any insight to share on that topic.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the real world, though... The lack of truthfulness shouldn't be overstated, however. The perspectives might be biased but history won't be rewritten in some grand fashion. That's conspiracy-theory-stuff like that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_chronology_(Fomenko)\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;New Chronology&quot;-conspiracy</a> from Russia:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The new chronology is a pseudohistorical theory proposed by Anatoly Fomenko who argues that events of antiquity generally attributed to the ancient civilizations of Rome, Greece and Egypt actually occurred during the Middle Ages, more than a thousand years later.<br /> <br /> The theory further proposes that world history prior to AD 1600 has been widely falsified to suit the interests of a number of different conspirators including the Vatican, the Holy Roman Empire, and the Russian House of Romanov, all working to obscure the &quot;true&quot; history of the world centered around a global empire called the &quot;Russian Horde&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That's how weird this would sound when you take actual Garou history and present a version that's just somebody making shit up. In a society with a shared identity and a belief that this identity is tied to a certain history, you can't just make up huge claims about that history contrary to common-held beliefs and knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T04:35:28-07:00","id":1542815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542803#post1542803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which again, is a very generous interpretation of things but nicely points out that the issue is not, &quot;Oral History is wrong&quot;, it is, &quot;The Garou are full of themselves and have deliberately refused to accept any alternative POVs or challenges to their supremacy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which actually kinda the tone for a section of the opening story for the Timeline section of the Up coming WtE.<br /> <br /> It involves a recently changed Child of Gaia theurge named Esme Leaping Ghost interviewing members of Dawn Tribes who has some strong words on the West cons record keeping traditions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> VOSK<br /> The process of finalizing official records in the Garou<br /> Nation are ultimately left to a small number of Talesingers<br /> to corroborate, and must undergo some degrees of biased<br /> review\u2014<br /> ESME<br /> Peer review?<br /> VOSK<br /> \u2014<b>in a way, yes. In this case, it\u2019s just one Garou that<br /> ultimately decides what is considered vital enough to be<br /> entered into the Silver Record.</b><br /> ESME<br /> Why just one?<br /> TORRANCE<br /> Westcon bullshit </div> </div> </div>The rest of the section is a dissection on the important of oral history followed by a recounting of a version the origin of the fera as a emphases on the importance of oral history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 09-28-2024, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T04:44:36-07:00","id":1542816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542805#post1542805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to the real world, though... The lack of truthfulness shouldn't be overstated, however. The perspectives might be biased but history won't be rewritten in some grand fashion. That's conspiracy-theory-stuff like that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_chronology_(Fomenko)\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;New Chronology&quot;-conspiracy</a> from Russia:</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree that I'm putting more things into it but you're also dealing with literal epochs of time as well.<br /> <br /> It's not about rewriting history but rewriting mythology when it comes to Garou oral history.<br /> <br /> And the thing is that mythology is RIGHT.<br /> <br /> But biased.<br /> <br /> When you're referring to Garou history and the confusion about it, it's going to be less &quot;we disagree that Runs Like Hell stole the Silver Crown in 1200 BC from the King of Babylon&quot; but &quot;And Grandfather Thunder sent a Flood to destroy the City of the First Vampire before the ground opened up to release the Hell Bison that breathed forth a million insects.&quot;<br /> <br /> Did it happen? IT COULD HAVE.<br /> <br /> It could also have been a metaphor originally or just a story told by some Galliard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T05:15:15-07:00","id":1542817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542816#post1542816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually agree that I'm putting more things into it but you're also dealing with literal epochs of time as well.<br /> <br /> It's not about rewriting history but rewriting mythology when it comes to Garou oral history.<br /> <br /> And the thing is that mythology is RIGHT.<br /> <br /> But biased.<br /> <br /> When you're referring to Garou history and the confusion about it, it's going to be less &quot;we disagree that Runs Like Hell stole the Silver Crown in 1200 BC from the King of Babylon&quot; but &quot;And Grandfather Thunder sent a Flood to destroy the City of the First Vampire before the ground opened up to release the Hell Bison that breathed forth a million insects.&quot;<br /> <br /> Did it happen? IT COULD HAVE.<br /> <br /> It could also have been a metaphor originally or just a story told by some Galliard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking about flexible stories the Glorantha setting I keep bring up history is explicitly written to a bit muddled and contradictory by it's author because he wants to capture the uncertainty of the myths that inspired the setting and wrote the setting metaphysics to reflect that.<br /> <br /> You see in Glorantha stores and the belief in them has real power and explicitly said to have the abilities to change reality and there's evidence in the books to actually happens many time. The players are enchrouged to come up with they own explanation on deliberately vague aspects of the setting because it's simply they're story. Hell even differences in the editions can be explained as different retelling of the setting story that have they own quarks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 09-28-2024, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T05:43:36-07:00","id":1542903,"title":"","content":"I feel one of the biggest signs how disjointed Shattered Nation and W5 as a whole is, is the way the outsider tribes are treated.<br /> <br /> BSDs are redeemable, all but one of the example plots are about that. Which would be fine if the text didn't also paint the tribe as much softer than in previous versions. Yet they still look like the typical BSDs. It also undercuts the whole 'you but evil' theme the tribe should have.<br /> <br /> It isn't helped by the way the CoF are treated in comparison. Even though the CoF are on the same side as the PCs, the example plots and the text still paint them as the worst of the worst. And also unredeemable, even though a big part of fighting fascism is to deradicalize its followers. I know the CoF are the favourite scapegoat of W5, but how can you tell a story of why extreme methods are bad when the CoF aren't allowed to be anything more than cartoon villains? Given how BSDs are written, it also erases the very point of CoF as the 'uses worse methods than the actual bad guys' group because the CoF are ALWAYS bad and BSDs are MOSTLY bad.<br /> <br /> The Stargazers then are treated as an afterthought, the text even stating they WOULD help the PCs if the PCs would only listen. The book deciding for the players how they would react is never a good thing. It isn't helped by the way W5 is supposed to be post-Nation, which would mean each tribe is doing their own thing anyway. Yet the book presents the post-Nation garou functioning mostly like the Nation garou, without offering an example how the Nation garou were different from the post-Nation garou.<br /> <br /> And, yet again, tribeless garou are not even mentioned. As if one cannot exist as a tribeless garou in the setting, even though they should be very common in the setting thanks to the shattered nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T07:04:03-07:00","id":1542905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542903#post1542903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I know the CoF are the favourite scapegoat of W5, but how can you tell a story of why extreme methods are bad when the CoF aren't allowed to be anything more than cartoon villains? Given how BSDs are written, it also erases the very point of CoF as the 'uses worse methods than the actual bad guys' group because the CoF are ALWAYS bad and BSDs are MOSTLY bad.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You know this brings to mind this post from the WtE thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542353#post1542353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, from my tumbler reading, they both have the same goals ( broadly speaking) they just have different ways of arriving at them....so they're not even as far apart as human political parties for the most part. They strike me more as Hard Left vs Soft Left.......they both want to shut down the puppy farm......but one is lobbying hard and sending dozens of Animal Welfare inspectors the other snuck in at night with a half dozen pickups and does a hard entry search and seizure home invasion...and possibly accidentally sets off a gas explosion as they leave...<br /> <br /> Jobs done either way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Ok, just realised this is basically also Cult of Fenris vs Gaian activities in W5........and whilst the former has likely more widespread positive flowthrough its very slow.....the other just feels a lot more satisfying and is immediately if somewhat limited in its usefulness....</div> </div> </div> </div>In short the CoF vs Gian conflict is echoed by the conflict between western vs eastern Concordat in WtE and the latter conflict is written with much more nuance than the former due the simple fact that both factions are playable and funnily enough the Get of Fenris is presented as one of the most tolerant tribe on the matter of kinfolk and warborn since the westcon writeup outright said they're the only tribe in the alliance that doesn't have any hang up about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542903#post1542903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.The Stargazers then are treated as an afterthought, the text even stating they WOULD help the PCs if the PCs would only listen. The book deciding for the players how they would react is never a good thing.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't a problem since they got absorbed by the Children of gaia shortly after the apocalypse<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1542903#post1542903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't helped by the way W5 is supposed to be post-Nation, which would mean each tribe is doing their own thing anyway. Yet the book presents the post-Nation garou functioning mostly like the Nation garou, without offering an example how the Nation garou were different from the post-Nation garou..</div> </div> </div> </div>You know it doesn't look good when WtE's version is competitively thriving despite the fact that the spetural ecosystem is so messed up that all the old cearn building and cleansing rites is basically Baine bait per Word of god and to reclaim a cearn the garou have and are welling to go though a lengthy process of a finding and clearing a ruinded cearn, plating a tending to a shard seed to grow to maturity before going on a tower defense sequence just so the cearn will regain a portion of it's splendor and by all accounts there are more then enough garou that welling to suffer the hard ships of the process it will heal gaia. Meanwhile W5 the seems to have just given up after a particularly rough fight. Talk about first would problems eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T11:03:26-07:00","id":1544894,"title":"","content":"Shattered nation is a book that justified W5 for me. Once again I understand the point of view of community that doesn't like new edition but after reading about what might happen with Albrecht , silver crown and his nearly death it convinced me why and how the w5 setting works. It is a story without happy ending and Werewolf the Apocalypse supposed to end this way.<br /> Curiously the player characters from older editions should be dead or survived maby broken like last Gaian king. That idea opens a lot.of doors for Gm.<br /> At the end I am a blind fanboy. That thought doesn't bother me at all. Surprisingly I'm happy with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 10-28-2024, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}